window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 16 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Select the figure from the options that can replace the question mark (?) and complete the given pattern.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विकल्पों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आकर दिए गए पैटर्न को पूरा कर सके।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the left half of the pattern the triangle points upwards with its inner lines; in the right half the same figure appears inverted, with the arrow pointing down.<br>The missing block must be this inverted figure placed below the top block, which is exactly option figure (4).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"पैटर्न के बाएँ भाग में त्रिभुज भीतरी रेखाओं के साथ ऊपर की ओर है; दाएँ भाग में वही आकृति उलटी है और तीर नीचे की ओर है।<br>गायब खाने में यही उलटी आकृति ऊपर के खाने के नीचे आनी चाहिए, जो विकल्प आकृति (4) में है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Two numbers are in the ratio 3:4. If their LCM is 240, find the numbers. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो संख्याएँ 3:4 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि उनका लघुत्तम समापवर्त्य (LCM) 240 है, तो संख्याएँ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"90, 120"},"2":{"en":"45, 60"},"3":{"en":"60, 80"},"4":{"en":"30, 40"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the numbers be 3x and 4x; their HCF is x, so LCM = 12x.<br>12x = 240 → x = 20<br>Numbers = 60 and 80<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60, 80.</b>","hi":"मान लें संख्याएँ 3x और 4x हैं; उनका HCF x है, इसलिए LCM = 12x।<br>12x = 240 → x = 20<br>संख्याएँ = 60 और 80<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60, 80 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the missing number: 6 : 208 :: 5 : ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए: 6 : 208 :: 5 : ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120"},"2":{"en":"125"},"3":{"en":"117"},"4":{"en":"110"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"6<sup>3</sup> − 8 = 216 − 8 = 208<br>Similarly 5<sup>3</sup> − 8 = 125 − 8 = 117<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 117.</b>","hi":"6<sup>3</sup> − 8 = 216 − 8 = 208<br>इसी प्रकार 5<sup>3</sup> − 8 = 125 − 8 = 117<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 117 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"The sequence of folding a piece of paper and the manner in which the folded paper has been cut is shown below. Choose a figure that would most closely resemble the unfolded form of the paper.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कागज़ को मोड़ने का क्रम तथा मुड़े हुए कागज़ को काटने का तरीका नीचे दर्शाया गया है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो कागज़ के खुलने पर उसके स्वरूप से सबसे अधिक मिलती हो।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The paper is folded twice, so the cut design appears at four places — two in each half, mirrored about the fold lines.<br>In option figure (4) all four impressions are exact mirror copies of the cut, so it is the unfolded form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"कागज़ दो बार मोड़ा गया है, इसलिए कटा हुआ डिज़ाइन चार स्थानों पर आएगा — प्रत्येक आधे भाग में दो, मोड़ की रेखाओं के अनुदिश दर्पण रूप में।<br>विकल्प आकृति (4) में चारों छापें कटाव की ठीक दर्पण प्रतियाँ हैं, अतः यही खुला हुआ रूप है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 'A' means '+', 'B' means '−', and 'C' means '×'<br><br>what is the value of the following expression?<br>5 A 3 C 2=? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 'A' का अर्थ '+', 'B' का अर्थ '−' और 'C' का अर्थ '×' है,<br><br>तो निम्नलिखित व्यंजक का मान क्या है?<br>5 A 3 C 2=? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Put the signs: 5 + 3 × 2<br>= 5 + 6 = 11<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 11.</b>","hi":"चिह्न रखने पर: 5 + 3 × 2<br>= 5 + 6 = 11<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 11 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a survey, 25 people like Tea, 20 like Coffee, and 10 like both. How many like only Tea? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सर्वेक्षण में 25 लोग चाय पसंद करते हैं, 20 कॉफ़ी पसंद करते हैं और 10 दोनों पसंद करते हैं। कितने लोग केवल चाय पसंद करते हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"13"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Only Tea = Tea − (Tea and Coffee) = 25 − 10<br>= 15<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15.</b>","hi":"केवल चाय = चाय − (चाय और कॉफ़ी दोनों) = 25 − 10<br>= 15<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If JOURNAL is coded as KPVSOBM, how is KPVSOBM coded? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि JOURNAL को KPVSOBM के रूप में कूटबद्ध किया जाता है, तो KPVSOBM को कैसे कूटबद्ध किया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"LQWTPCN"},"2":{"en":"LQWUPCN"},"3":{"en":"LQWTPCO"},"4":{"en":"LQWTPCM"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"J + 1 = K, O + 1 = P, U + 1 = V, R + 1 = S, N + 1 = O, A + 1 = B, L + 1 = M — each letter moves one step forward.<br>So KPVSOBM → LQWTPCN<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): LQWTPCN.</b>","hi":"J + 1 = K, O + 1 = P, U + 1 = V, R + 1 = S, N + 1 = O, A + 1 = B, L + 1 = M — प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ता है।<br>अतः KPVSOBM → LQWTPCN<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): LQWTPCN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br><br>121, 144, 169, 196, 225, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रृंखला में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br><br>121, 144, 169, 196, 225, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"255"},"2":{"en":"256"},"3":{"en":"275"},"4":{"en":"289"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"121 = 11<sup>2</sup>, 144 = 12<sup>2</sup>, 169 = 13<sup>2</sup>, 196 = 14<sup>2</sup>, 225 = 15<sup>2</sup><br>Next = 16<sup>2</sup> = 256<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 256.</b>","hi":"121 = 11<sup>2</sup>, 144 = 12<sup>2</sup>, 169 = 13<sup>2</sup>, 196 = 14<sup>2</sup>, 225 = 15<sup>2</sup><br>अगली = 16<sup>2</sup> = 256<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 256 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"WRITING\" is written as \"HOJUJSX.\" How will \"READERS\" be written? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"WRITING\" को \"HOJUJSX.\" लिखा जाता है। \"READERS\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TSEFBFS"},"2":{"en":"TSFFBES"},"3":{"en":"TSFEBFS"},"4":{"en":"TSEEBFS"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"WRITING written backwards is GNITIRW; adding 1 to each letter gives HOJUJSX ✓<br>READERS backwards = SREDAER → TSFEBFS<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): TSFEBFS.</b>","hi":"WRITING को उलटा लिखने पर GNITIRW मिलता है; प्रत्येक अक्षर में 1 जोड़ने पर HOJUJSX ✓<br>READERS उलटा = SREDAER → TSFEBFS<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): TSFEBFS है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In this following question, four words have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and the fourth one is different. Choose odd one out. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"इस प्रश्न में चार शब्द दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और चौथा भिन्न है। विषम शब्द चुनिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lok Sabha","hi":"लोकसभा"},"2":{"en":"Rajya Sabha","hi":"राज्यसभा"},"3":{"en":"Legislative Assembly","hi":"विधानसभा"},"4":{"en":"Supreme Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha and Legislative Assembly are all legislatures.<br>The Supreme Court is a judicial body, so it is different.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Supreme Court.</b>","hi":"लोकसभा, राज्यसभा और विधानसभा सभी विधायिकाएँ हैं।<br>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय एक न्यायिक निकाय है, इसलिए यह भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): सर्वोच्च न्यायालय है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If A + B means A is the brother of B, A ÷ B means A is the father of B, and A × B means A is the sister of B — which of the following means M is the uncle of P? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि A + B का अर्थ है कि A, B का भाई है, A ÷ B का अर्थ है कि A, B का पिता है, और A × B का अर्थ है कि A, B की बहन है — तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा दर्शाता है कि M, P का चाचा है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"N × P + M"},"2":{"en":"M + S ÷ R ÷ P"},"3":{"en":"M + N ÷ P"},"4":{"en":"M + K + T × P"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">N+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">P</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>M + N ÷ P: M is the brother of P's father N, so M is P's uncle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): M + N ÷ P.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">N+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">P</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>M + N ÷ P: M, P के पिता N का भाई है, अतः M, P का चाचा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): M + N ÷ P है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>HNA, FOY, DPW, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला में पैटर्न का अध्ययन करें और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>HNA, FOY, DPW, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BQU"},"2":{"en":"BPU"},"3":{"en":"BQT"},"4":{"en":"BQV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letter: H → F → D → B (−2 each)<br>Second letter: N → O → P → Q (+1 each)<br>Third letter: A → Y → W → U (−2 each)<br>Next set = BQU<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): BQU.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर: H → F → D → B (प्रत्येक −2)<br>दूसरा अक्षर: N → O → P → Q (प्रत्येक +1)<br>तीसरा अक्षर: A → Y → W → U (प्रत्येक −2)<br>अगला समूह = BQU<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): BQU है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"From the letters of the word ‘BLACKBOARD’, identify which of the given options cannot be formed, using each letter only as many times as it appears in the original word. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द ‘BLACKBOARD’ के अक्षरों से पहचानें कि दिए गए विकल्पों में से कौन-सा नहीं बनाया जा सकता, प्रत्येक अक्षर का उपयोग केवल उतनी ही बार करते हुए जितनी बार वह मूल शब्द में आता है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BACKLOAD"},"2":{"en":"ABROAD"},"3":{"en":"BLOCK"},"4":{"en":"CLOCK"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"BLACKBOARD has B twice, A twice and C only once.<br>CLOCK needs C two times, so it cannot be formed from these letters.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): CLOCK.</b>","hi":"BLACKBOARD में B दो बार, A दो बार तथा C केवल एक बार है।<br>CLOCK के लिए C दो बार चाहिए, इसलिए यह इन अक्षरों से नहीं बनाया जा सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): CLOCK है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which centre code does not follow the pattern of \"three digits in ascending order\"? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा सेंटर कोड \"तीन अंक आरोही क्रम में\" के पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"123A"},"2":{"en":"456B"},"3":{"en":"785C"},"4":{"en":"234D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"123, 456 and 234 are in ascending order of their digits.<br>In 785 the digits decrease from 8 to 5, so this code does not follow the pattern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 785C.</b>","hi":"123, 456 और 234 के अंक आरोही क्रम में हैं।<br>785 में अंक 8 से 5 की ओर घटते हैं, इसलिए यह कोड पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 785C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानें और उसी के अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"21"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Row 1: 5 × 4 = 20 and 8 × 4 = 32<br>Row 2: 3 × 7 = 21 and 6 × 7 = 42<br>Row 3: 7 × 5 = 35, so ? = 2 × 5 = 10<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10.</b>","hi":"पंक्ति 1: 5 × 4 = 20 और 8 × 4 = 32<br>पंक्ति 2: 3 × 7 = 21 और 6 × 7 = 42<br>पंक्ति 3: 7 × 5 = 35, अतः ? = 2 × 5 = 10<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 14#3 = 45 and 18#4 = 58, find the value of 22#5. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 14#3 = 45 और 18#4 = 58 है, तो 22#5 का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"71"},"2":{"en":"68"},"3":{"en":"76"},"4":{"en":"82"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"14 × 3 + 3 = 42 + 3 = 45 ✓<br>18 × 3 + 4 = 54 + 4 = 58 ✓<br>So a#b = a × 3 + b → 22 × 3 + 5 = 66 + 5 = 71<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 71.</b>","hi":"14 × 3 + 3 = 42 + 3 = 45 ✓<br>18 × 3 + 4 = 54 + 4 = 58 ✓<br>अतः a#b = a × 3 + b → 22 × 3 + 5 = 66 + 5 = 71<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 71 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A boy says to his friend, “Look at the sign on the road; it indicates that this is a one-way road.”<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Vehicles are permitted to move only in the direction indicated by the arrow on the signboard.<br>II. The boy is familiar with traffic signs. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़ें और उसे सत्य मानें। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच करें और निर्धारित करें कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हों, कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक लड़का अपने मित्र से कहता है, \"सड़क पर लगा संकेत देखो; यह दर्शाता है कि यह एकतरफ़ा सड़क है।\"<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. वाहनों को केवल साइनबोर्ड पर तीर द्वारा दर्शाई दिशा में ही चलने की अनुमति है।<br>II. लड़का यातायात संकेतों से परिचित है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A one-way sign does mean that traffic moves only in the arrow’s direction, so I follows.<br>The boy reads the sign correctly, which shows he knows traffic signs, so II follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both Conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"एकतरफ़ा संकेत का अर्थ है कि यातायात केवल तीर की दिशा में चलता है, इसलिए I निकलता है।<br>लड़का संकेत सही पढ़ता है, जो दर्शाता है कि वह यातायात संकेतों को जानता है, इसलिए II निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The school has decided to increase the number of library books and extend library hours to encourage reading habits among students.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The school wishes to promote reading among students.<br>II. The school believes greater access to books may encourage reading habits. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़ें और उसे सत्य मानें। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच करें और निर्धारित करें कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हों, कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>विद्यालय ने छात्रों में पठन-आदतें बढ़ाने के लिए पुस्तकालय की पुस्तकों की संख्या बढ़ाने और पुस्तकालय का समय बढ़ाने का निर्णय लिया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. विद्यालय छात्रों में पठन को बढ़ावा देना चाहता है।<br>II. विद्यालय मानता है कि पुस्तकों तक अधिक पहुँच से पठन-आदतें बढ़ सकती हैं। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The stated aim itself is to encourage reading habits, so I follows directly.<br>More books and longer hours are given as the means to that aim, so II also follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Both conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"कथन का लक्ष्य ही पठन-आदतें बढ़ाना है, इसलिए I सीधे निकलता है।<br>अधिक पुस्तकें और अधिक समय इस लक्ष्य के साधन बताए गए हैं, इसलिए II भी निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Pahi is exploring extracurricular opportunities offered by her school. She is particularly drawn to activities that encourage artistic expression, imagination, and hands-on creativity. At the same time, she has little interest in physically demanding or highly competitive sports.<br><br>Considering her interests and preferences, which of the following clubs would be the most suitable for her to join? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पाही अपने विद्यालय द्वारा दिए जाने वाले पाठ्येतर अवसरों की खोज कर रही है। वह विशेष रूप से उन गतिविधियों की ओर आकर्षित है जो कलात्मक अभिव्यक्ति, कल्पना और प्रत्यक्ष रचनात्मकता को बढ़ावा देती हैं। साथ ही, शारीरिक रूप से कठिन या अत्यधिक प्रतिस्पर्धी खेलों में उसकी रुचि बहुत कम है।<br><br>उसकी रुचियों और पसंद को ध्यान में रखते हुए, निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा क्लब उसके जुड़ने के लिए सबसे उपयुक्त होगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An Art and Craft Club that focuses on painting, sketching, design, and creative projects.","hi":"एक कला एवं शिल्प क्लब जो चित्रकला, रेखाचित्र, डिज़ाइन और रचनात्मक परियोजनाओं पर केंद्रित है।"},"2":{"en":"A Boxing Club that emphasizes combat techniques, endurance, and competitive matches.","hi":"एक बॉक्सिंग क्लब जो युद्ध तकनीक, सहनशक्ति और प्रतिस्पर्धी मुकाबलों पर ज़ोर देता है।"},"3":{"en":"A Football Club that requires teamwork, athletic training, and regular competitive play.","hi":"एक फ़ुटबॉल क्लब जिसमें टीम भावना, खेल प्रशिक्षण और नियमित प्रतिस्पर्धी खेल आवश्यक हैं।"},"4":{"en":"A Wrestling Club that involves physical conditioning, grappling skills, and tournament participation.","hi":"एक कुश्ती क्लब जिसमें शारीरिक फिटनेस, पकड़-तकनीक और प्रतियोगिताओं में भागीदारी शामिल है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"She wants artistic, imaginative and hands-on creative work and no physically demanding or competitive sport.<br>Only the Art and Craft Club matches all her preferences; the other three clubs are demanding, competitive sports.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): An Art and Craft Club that focuses on painting, sketching, design, and creative projects.</b>","hi":"वह कलात्मक, कल्पनाशील और प्रत्यक्ष रचनात्मक कार्य चाहती है तथा शारीरिक रूप से कठिन या प्रतिस्पर्धी खेल नहीं चाहती।<br>केवल कला एवं शिल्प क्लब उसकी सभी पसंद से मेल खाता है; शेष तीन क्लब कठिन, प्रतिस्पर्धी खेल हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): एक कला एवं शिल्प क्लब जो चित्रकला, रेखाचित्र, डिज़ाइन और रचनात्मक परियोजनाओं पर केंद्रित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Only a few mirrors are combs.<br>Some combs are brushes.<br>No brush is a dryer.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All mirrors can be combs is a possibility.<br>II. All combs can be mirrors is a possibility. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन दिए गए हैं, जिनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानें, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और निर्धारित करें कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केवल कुछ दर्पण कंघे हैं।<br>कुछ कंघे ब्रश हैं।<br>कोई भी ब्रश ड्रायर नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी दर्पण कंघे हो सकते हैं, यह संभावना है।<br>II. सभी कंघे दर्पण हो सकते हैं, यह संभावना है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Either conclusion I or conclusion II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"“Only a few mirrors are combs” means some mirrors are not combs, so all mirrors cannot be combs. I does not follow.<br>Nothing stops all combs from being mirrors; the combs that are brushes still stay inside mirrors. II follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"“केवल कुछ दर्पण कंघे हैं” का अर्थ है कि कुछ दर्पण कंघे नहीं हैं, इसलिए सभी दर्पण कंघे नहीं हो सकते। I नहीं निकलता।<br>सभी कंघों के दर्पण होने में कोई बाधा नहीं; जो कंघे ब्रश हैं वे भी दर्पण के भीतर रहते हैं। II निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Identify the Venn diagram that accurately depicts the logical relationships between the given categories.<br>Snake, Reptiles, Lizard [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह वेन आरेख पहचानें जो दी गई श्रेणियों के बीच तार्किक संबंधों को सही रूप से दर्शाता है।<br>साँप, सरीसृप, छिपकली [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Both snake and lizard are reptiles, and no snake is a lizard.<br>So the two separate circles of snake and lizard must lie inside the circle of reptiles — option figure (4).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"साँप और छिपकली दोनों सरीसृप हैं, और कोई साँप छिपकली नहीं है।<br>अतः साँप और छिपकली के दो अलग वृत्त सरीसृप के वृत्त के भीतर होने चाहिए — विकल्प आकृति (4)।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has decided to offer tax incentives to companies that set up manufacturing plants in rural areas to stimulate local employment.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Companies are likely to be motivated by financial incentives to expand their operations into rural regions.<br>II. There is a lack of adequate manufacturing infrastructure currently available in urban regions. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़ें। निर्धारित करें कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>स्थानीय रोज़गार को प्रोत्साहित करने के लिए सरकार ने ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में विनिर्माण संयंत्र स्थापित करने वाली कंपनियों को कर प्रोत्साहन देने का निर्णय लिया है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. कंपनियाँ अपने कार्य ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में बढ़ाने के लिए वित्तीय प्रोत्साहनों से प्रेरित हो सकती हैं।<br>II. वर्तमान में शहरी क्षेत्रों में पर्याप्त विनिर्माण अधोसंरचना का अभाव है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Tax incentives are offered only because companies are expected to respond to money benefits. I is implicit.<br>The statement says nothing about urban infrastructure, so II is not implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"कर प्रोत्साहन इसलिए दिए जा रहे हैं क्योंकि कंपनियाँ आर्थिक लाभ पर प्रतिक्रिया देंगी। I निहित है।<br>कथन शहरी अधोसंरचना के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहता, इसलिए II निहित नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अनुमान I निहित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Choose the alternative which most closely resembles the mirror image of the given combination when mirror is placed at the right side of the image.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए संयोजन के दर्पण प्रतिबिंब से सबसे अधिक मिलता हो, जब दर्पण को चित्र के दाईं ओर रखा जाए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The mirror is on the right, so the order of the characters is reversed and each character turns left to right.<br>5 g s d f n c k becomes k c n f d s g 5 with all characters laterally inverted, which is option figure (4).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"दर्पण दाईं ओर है, इसलिए अक्षरों का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर बाएँ-दाएँ पलट जाता है।<br>5 g s d f n c k का k c n f d s g 5 बनता है और सभी अक्षर पार्श्व रूप से उलटे होते हैं, जो विकल्प आकृति (4) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q23_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Choose the alternative which most closely resembles the mirror image of the given combination when mirror is placed at the right side of the image.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए संयोजन के दर्पण प्रतिबिंब से सबसे अधिक मिलता हो, जब दर्पण को चित्र के दाईं ओर रखा जाए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"With the mirror on the right, the combination 7 D I S C H A R G E 5 is read from the last character and every character is laterally inverted.<br>Option figure (4) shows this reversed and inverted form correctly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"दर्पण दाईं ओर होने पर संयोजन 7 D I S C H A R G E 5 अंतिम अक्षर से पढ़ा जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर पार्श्व रूप से उलट जाता है।<br>विकल्प आकृति (4) यह उलटा और पलटा हुआ रूप सही दर्शाती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q24_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures which will continue the same series as established by the five Problem Figures.<br>Problem Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उत्तर आकृतियों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो पाँच समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रृंखला को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br>समस्या आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the problem figures the three symbols move one position each step, and the circle and the cross swap places in every alternate figure.<br>Continuing the movement from figure E gives answer figure 1.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"समस्या आकृतियों में तीनों चिह्न प्रत्येक चरण में एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं और हर दूसरी आकृति में वृत्त तथा क्रॉस स्थान बदलते हैं।<br>आकृति E से वही गति आगे बढ़ाने पर उत्तर आकृति 1 प्राप्त होती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073106","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"After consolidating his power, which grand title did Sultan Ghiyasuddin Balban assume? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अपनी सत्ता को सुदृढ़ करने के बाद सुल्तान गयासुद्दीन बलबन ने कौन-सी भव्य उपाधि धारण की? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Zill-e-Ilahi","hi":"जिल्ल-ए-इलाही"},"2":{"en":"Tuti-e-Hind","hi":"तूती-ए-हिंद"},"3":{"en":"Kaisar-e-Hind","hi":"कैसर-ए-हिंद"},"4":{"en":"Din-e-Ilahi","hi":"दीन-ए-इलाही"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Zill-e-Ilahi</b><br><b>Balban</b>, the powerful ruler of the <b>Mamluk (Slave) dynasty</b>, assumed the title <b>Zill-e-Ilahi</b>, meaning the <b>shadow of God on earth</b>, to raise the prestige of the sultanate.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Balban ruled from <b>1266 to 1287</b> and was a member of the <b>Chalisa (Chalgan) group</b> of Turkish nobles earlier.<br>• He introduced the <b>Persian Nauroz festival</b>, the <b>sijda and paibos</b> (prostration before the king) and a strict court etiquette to emphasise the divine right of kings.<br>• He created a strong <b>spy system</b>, reorganised the army and the <b>iqta</b> system, and crushed the <b>Mewati rebels</b> and the dacoits of the Ganga-Yamuna doab.<br>• <b>Din-e-Ilahi</b> was the religion propounded by <b>Akbar</b> in 1582, and <b>Tuti-e-Hind</b> (parrot of India) was the title of the poet <b>Amir Khusrau</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जिल्ल-ए-इलाही</b><br><b>बलबन</b>, जो <b>गुलाम वंश</b> का शक्तिशाली शासक था, ने सल्तनत की प्रतिष्ठा बढ़ाने के लिए <b>जिल्ल-ए-इलाही</b> अर्थात <b>ईश्वर की छाया</b> उपाधि धारण की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बलबन ने <b>1266 से 1287</b> तक शासन किया तथा पहले तुर्की अमीरों के <b>चालीसा (चालगान) गुट</b> का सदस्य था।<br>• उसने <b>फारसी नौरोज</b> उत्सव, <b>सिजदा तथा पैबोस</b> (राजा के समक्ष झुकना) तथा कठोर दरबारी शिष्टाचार आरंभ किया, जिससे राजा के दैवीय अधिकार पर बल पड़ा।<br>• उसने सुदृढ़ <b>गुप्तचर व्यवस्था</b> बनाई, सेना तथा <b>इक्ता</b> प्रणाली का पुनर्गठन किया और <b>मेवाती विद्रोहियों</b> तथा गंगा-यमुना दोआब के डाकुओं को दबाया।<br>• <b>दीन-ए-इलाही</b> 1582 में <b>अकबर</b> द्वारा चलाया गया धर्म था तथा <b>तूती-ए-हिंद</b> (हिंद का तोता) कवि <b>अमीर खुसरो</b> की उपाधि थी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073107","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"Which site in Tamil Nadu has produced notable evidence of the South Indian Neolithic culture? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तमिलनाडु का कौन-सा स्थल दक्षिण भारतीय नवपाषाण संस्कृति के उल्लेखनीय साक्ष्य प्रदान करता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Utnur","hi":"उटनूर"},"2":{"en":"Kupgal","hi":"कुपगल"},"3":{"en":"Paiyyampalli","hi":"पैयमपल्ली"},"4":{"en":"Sanganakallu","hi":"संगनकल्लू"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Paiyyampalli</b><br><b>Paiyyampalli</b> in <b>Tamil Nadu</b> is an important <b>Neolithic site</b> that has yielded evidence of the South Indian Neolithic culture, including stone axes, pottery and ash mounds.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• South Indian Neolithic sites include <b>Paiyyampalli, Terdal, Hallur, Brahmagiri, Sanganakallu, Tekkalakota and Utnur</b>.<br>• The culture is marked by <b>ash mounds</b>, polished stone <b>celts (axes and adzes)</b>, hand-made pottery and the domestication of <b>cattle and millets</b>.<br>• <b>Utnur</b> in Telangana and <b>Kupgal</b> in Karnataka are known respectively for ash mounds and rock art, and <b>Sanganakallu</b> for a large Neolithic settlement.<br>• The South Indian Neolithic is dated roughly between <b>3000 and 1000 BCE</b> and marks the beginning of settled life and animal herding in the peninsula.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पैयमपल्ली</b><br><b>तमिलनाडु</b> का <b>पैयमपल्ली</b> एक महत्वपूर्ण <b>नवपाषाण स्थल</b> है, जहाँ से पत्थर की कुल्हाड़ियाँ, मृदभांड तथा राख के टीले आदि दक्षिण भारतीय नवपाषाण संस्कृति के साक्ष्य प्राप्त हुए हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दक्षिण भारतीय नवपाषाण स्थलों में <b>पैयमपल्ली, तेरदाल, हल्लूर, ब्रह्मगिरि, संगनकल्लू, तेक्कलकोटा तथा उटनूर</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• इस संस्कृति की विशेषताएँ <b>राख के टीले</b>, चमकाए गए पत्थर के <b>सेल्ट (कुल्हाड़ी एवं कुदाल)</b>, हस्तनिर्मित मृदभांड तथा <b>पशु एवं मोटे अनाज</b> का पालन हैं।<br>• तेलंगाना का <b>उटनूर</b> राख के टीलों तथा कर्नाटक का <b>कुपगल</b> शैलचित्रों के लिए तथा <b>संगनकल्लू</b> विशाल नवपाषाण बस्ती के लिए जाना जाता है।<br>• दक्षिण भारतीय नवपाषाण काल लगभग <b>3000 से 1000 ईसा पूर्व</b> माना जाता है और यह प्रायद्वीप में स्थायी जीवन तथा पशुपालन के आरंभ का प्रतीक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073108","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"In which Neolithic site did people live in deep pits to stay warm during the cold winter? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस नवपाषाण स्थल के लोग कड़ाके की सर्दी में गर्म रहने के लिए गहरे गड्ढों में रहते थे? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Burzahom","hi":"बुर्जहोम"},"2":{"en":"Mehrgarh","hi":"मेहरगढ़"},"3":{"en":"Palavoy","hi":"पलावॉय"},"4":{"en":"Brahmagiri","hi":"ब्रह्मगिरि"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Burzahom</b><br>At <b>Burzahom</b> in the <b>Kashmir valley</b>, Neolithic people dug <b>pit dwellings</b>, with steps leading down, to protect themselves from the severe cold of winter.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Burzahom is dated about <b>3000 to 1500 BCE</b> and also yielded <b>dog burials with human burials</b>, showing an early human-animal relationship.<br>• Other important sites are <b>Gufkral (Kashmir), Mehrgarh (Balochistan), Chirand (Bihar), Koldihwa and Mahagara (Uttar Pradesh)</b>.<br>• <b>Mehrgarh</b> is among the earliest farming sites in South Asia, with evidence of <b>wheat and barley</b> cultivation and mud-brick houses.<br>• <b>Brahmagiri</b> in Karnataka is famous for <b>Neolithic to Megalithic</b> cultural phases, and <b>Palavoy</b> in Andhra Pradesh is an ash-mound site.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बुर्जहोम</b><br><b>कश्मीर घाटी</b> के <b>बुर्जहोम</b> में नवपाषाण कालीन लोगों ने सर्दी की कड़ाके की ठंड से बचने के लिए सीढ़ियों वाले <b>गड्ढों में निर्मित आवास</b> बनाए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बुर्जहोम का काल लगभग <b>3000 से 1500 ईसा पूर्व</b> है तथा यहाँ <b>मानव कब्रों के साथ कुत्तों के दफन</b> के साक्ष्य मिले, जो मानव-पशु संबंध का प्रारंभिक प्रमाण है।<br>• अन्य महत्वपूर्ण स्थल हैं <b>गुफक्राल (कश्मीर), मेहरगढ़ (बलोचिस्तान), चिरांद (बिहार), कोलडिहवा तथा महगड़ा (उत्तर प्रदेश)</b>।<br>• <b>मेहरगढ़</b> दक्षिण एशिया के आरंभिक कृषि स्थलों में है, जहाँ <b>गेहूँ एवं जौ</b> की खेती तथा कच्ची ईंट के घरों के साक्ष्य मिले।<br>• कर्नाटक का <b>ब्रह्मगिरि</b> <b>नवपाषाण से महापाषाण</b> चरणों के लिए तथा आंध्र प्रदेश का <b>पलावॉय</b> राख-टीले स्थल के रूप में प्रसिद्ध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073109","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Rivers","question":{"en":"Which significant Peninsular River is known for forming an estuary at its mouth instead of a delta? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी महत्वपूर्ण प्रायद्वीपीय नदी अपने मुख पर डेल्टा के स्थान पर जलडमरूमध्य (एस्चुअरी) बनाने के लिए जानी जाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ganga","hi":"गंगा"},"2":{"en":"Godavari","hi":"गोदावरी"},"3":{"en":"Narmada","hi":"नर्मदा"},"4":{"en":"Padma","hi":"पद्मा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Narmada</b><br>The <b>Narmada</b> flows through a <b>rift valley</b> between the Vindhya and Satpura ranges and forms an <b>estuary</b> (not a delta) at its mouth in the Gulf of Khambhat.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Narmada</b> rises from <b>Amarkantak</b> and flows west into the <b>Arabian Sea</b>, with almost no tributaries along its course.<br>• Because it carries <b>little silt</b> in a steep rift valley, deposition at the mouth is small, so an estuary is formed.<br>• The <b>Tapi</b> is the other major west-flowing peninsular river that forms an estuary, while the <b>Mahi and Sabarmati</b> form small deltas.<br>• East-flowing rivers such as the <b>Godavari, Krishna, Kaveri and Mahanadi</b> form large deltas on the Bay of Bengal coast, and the <b>Ganga</b> forms the Sunderbans delta.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नर्मदा</b><br><b>नर्मदा</b> विंध्य तथा सतपुड़ा श्रेणियों के बीच <b>भ्रंश घाटी</b> से बहकर खंभात की खाड़ी में <b>जलडमरूमध्य</b> बनाती है, डेल्टा नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नर्मदा</b> <b>अमरकंटक</b> से निकलकर पश्चिम की ओर <b>अरब सागर</b> में गिरती है और इसके मार्ग में लगभग कोई सहायक नदी नहीं मिलती।<br>• तीव्र भ्रंश घाटी में यह <b>कम गाद</b> ले जाती है, अतः मुख पर निक्षेपण कम होने से जलडमरूमध्य बनता है।<br>• <b>तापी</b> दूसरी प्रमुख पश्चिम-वाहिनी प्रायद्वीपीय नदी है जो जलडमरूमध्य बनाती है, जबकि <b>माही तथा साबरमती</b> छोटे डेल्टा बनाती हैं।<br>• पूर्व-वाहिनी नदियाँ <b>गोदावरी, कृष्णा, कावेरी तथा महानदी</b> बंगाल की खाड़ी तट पर बड़े डेल्टा बनाती हैं तथा <b>गंगा</b> सुंदरबन डेल्टा बनाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073110","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Which physical quantity is represented by the slope of a distance-time graph? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दूरी-समय ग्राफ की प्रवणता किस भौतिक राशि को दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Speed","hi":"चाल"},"2":{"en":"Force","hi":"बल"},"3":{"en":"Acceleration","hi":"त्वरण"},"4":{"en":"Displacement","hi":"विस्थापन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Speed</b><br>The <b>slope of a distance-time graph</b> gives <b>distance divided by time</b>, which is <b>speed</b>. A steeper line means a higher speed.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• For a straight-line graph, the speed is <b>uniform</b>; for a curved graph, the slope at a point gives the <b>instantaneous speed</b>.<br>• A <b>horizontal line</b> in a distance-time graph means the object is at <b>rest</b>, and a line bending towards the time axis shows <b>decreasing speed</b>.<br>• In a <b>velocity-time graph</b> the slope gives <b>acceleration</b> and the area under the graph gives <b>displacement</b>.<br>• Speed is a <b>scalar</b>, while velocity is a <b>vector</b> quantity; the SI unit of both is <b>metre per second</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – चाल</b><br><b>दूरी-समय ग्राफ की प्रवणता</b> <b>दूरी को समय से भाग</b> देकर प्राप्त होती है, जो <b>चाल</b> है। अधिक ढाल का अर्थ अधिक चाल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सरल रेखीय ग्राफ में चाल <b>एकसमान</b> होती है, जबकि वक्र ग्राफ में किसी बिंदु की प्रवणता <b>तात्कालिक चाल</b> देती है।<br>• दूरी-समय ग्राफ में <b>क्षैतिज रेखा</b> वस्तु के <b>विराम</b> को तथा समय अक्ष की ओर मुड़ती रेखा <b>घटती चाल</b> को दर्शाती है।<br>• <b>वेग-समय ग्राफ</b> में प्रवणता <b>त्वरण</b> देती है तथा ग्राफ के नीचे का क्षेत्रफल <b>विस्थापन</b> देता है।<br>• चाल <b>अदिश</b> राशि है, जबकि वेग <b>सदिश</b> राशि है; दोनों की SI इकाई <b>मीटर प्रति सेकंड</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073111","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of districts in West Bengal is known for possessing mica reserves? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पश्चिम बंगाल के निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से जिलों के युग्म में अभ्रक भंडार पाए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kolkata and Howrah","hi":"कोलकाता तथा हावड़ा"},"2":{"en":"Purulia and Bankura","hi":"पुरुलिया तथा बांकुड़ा"},"3":{"en":"Darjeeling and Jalpaiguri","hi":"दार्जिलिंग तथा जलपाईगुड़ी"},"4":{"en":"Medinipur and Bardhaman","hi":"मेदिनीपुर तथा बर्धमान"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Purulia and Bankura</b><br>In West Bengal, <b>mica</b> reserves are found mainly in <b>Purulia</b> and <b>Bankura</b> districts, which lie on the eastern edge of the Chota Nagpur plateau.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India is one of the world's leading producers of <b>sheet mica</b>, with the main belt in <b>Jharkhand, Andhra Pradesh, Rajasthan, Odisha, Maharashtra and West Bengal</b>.<br>• Mica is valued for its <b>excellent dielectric strength, low power loss and heat resistance</b>, and is used in electrical insulators and electronics.<br>• <b>Koderma (Jharkhand)</b> is called the <b>mica capital of India</b>, and the <b>Nellore belt (Andhra Pradesh)</b> is famous for high-quality mica.<br>• West Bengal's <b>coal</b> comes from Raniganj and its <b>iron ore</b> mainly from Purulia and Bankura, which also hold <b>apatite and china clay</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पुरुलिया तथा बांकुड़ा</b><br>पश्चिम बंगाल में <b>अभ्रक</b> के भंडार मुख्यतः <b>पुरुलिया</b> तथा <b>बांकुड़ा</b> जिलों में मिलते हैं, जो छोटा नागपुर पठार के पूर्वी किनारे पर स्थित हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत विश्व के प्रमुख <b>शीट अभ्रक</b> उत्पादकों में है; मुख्य पट्टी <b>झारखंड, आंध्र प्रदेश, राजस्थान, ओडिशा, महाराष्ट्र तथा पश्चिम बंगाल</b> में है।<br>• अभ्रक <b>विद्युतरोधी शक्ति, कम ऊर्जा हानि तथा ऊष्मा प्रतिरोध</b> के कारण महत्वपूर्ण है और विद्युत विच्छेदकों तथा इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स में प्रयुक्त होता है।<br>• झारखंड का <b>कोडरमा</b> <b>भारत की अभ्रक राजधानी</b> कहलाता है तथा <b>नेल्लोर पट्टी (आंध्र प्रदेश)</b> उच्च गुणवत्ता के अभ्रक के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• पश्चिम बंगाल का <b>कोयला</b> रानीगंज से तथा <b>लौह अयस्क</b> मुख्यतः पुरुलिया एवं बांकुड़ा से मिलता है, जहाँ <b>अपेटाइट तथा चीनी मिट्टी</b> भी पाई जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073112","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Chumpha Festival is celebrated in which Indian state? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चुम्फा उत्सव भारत के किस राज्य में मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nagaland","hi":"नगालैंड"},"2":{"en":"Manipur","hi":"मणिपुर"},"3":{"en":"Meghalaya","hi":"मेघालय"},"4":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिजोरम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Manipur</b><br><b>Chumpha</b> is a festival of the <b>Tangkhul Naga</b> community of <b>Manipur</b>, celebrated as a festival of <b>thanksgiving</b> after the harvest.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The festival is marked by <b>community feasts, traditional dances and songs</b>, and prayers for a good harvest in the coming year.<br>• Manipur's other major festivals are <b>Yaoshang (Holi), Ningol Chakouba, Lai Haraoba, Kut and Sangai Festival</b>.<br>• The <b>Tangkhul</b> are a major Naga tribe of the <b>Ukhrul</b> district of Manipur.<br>• Nagaland is known for the <b>Hornbill Festival</b>, Meghalaya for <b>Wangala and Nongkrem</b> and Mizoram for <b>Chapchar Kut</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मणिपुर</b><br><b>चुम्फा</b> <b>मणिपुर</b> के <b>तांगखुल नागा</b> समुदाय का उत्सव है, जो फसल कटाई के बाद <b>धन्यवाद</b> के रूप में मनाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस उत्सव में <b>सामूहिक भोज, पारंपरिक नृत्य एवं गीत</b> तथा आगामी वर्ष की अच्छी फसल की प्रार्थना होती है।<br>• मणिपुर के अन्य प्रमुख उत्सव हैं <b>योशांग (होली), निंगोल चाकौबा, लाई हराओबा, कुट तथा संगाई महोत्सव</b>।<br>• <b>तांगखुल</b> मणिपुर के <b>उखरुल</b> जिले की प्रमुख नागा जनजाति है।<br>• नगालैंड <b>हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव</b>, मेघालय <b>वांगला तथा नोंगक्रेम</b> तथा मिजोरम <b>चापचर कुट</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073113","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"In March 2026, Arundhati Reddy was recognized for which achievement? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मार्च 2026 में अरुंधति रेड्डी को किस उपलब्धि के लिए सम्मानित किया गया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arjuna Award","hi":"अर्जुन पुरस्कार"},"2":{"en":"International Cricket Council (ICC) Women's Player of the Month","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय क्रिकेट परिषद (ICC) की महिला माह का सर्वश्रेष्ठ खिलाड़ी"},"3":{"en":"Twenty20 (T20) series win as captain","hi":"कप्तान के रूप में टी20 श्रृंखला विजय"},"4":{"en":"One Day International (ODI) world record","hi":"एकदिवसीय अंतर्राष्ट्रीय (ODI) विश्व रिकॉर्ड"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – International Cricket Council (ICC) Women's Player of the Month</b><br>In <b>March 2026</b>, the Indian cricketer <b>Arundhati Reddy</b> was recognised as the <b>ICC Women's Player of the Month</b> for her performances.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>ICC Player of the Month</b> award was introduced in <b>January 2021</b> and is decided by an independent voting panel.<br>• Arundhati Reddy is a <b>right-arm medium pace bowler</b> from Hyderabad who has played for India in all three formats.<br>• She was part of India's squad in the <b>ICC Women's Cricket World Cup 2025</b>, hosted by India and Sri Lanka.<br>• The <b>Arjuna Award</b> is given by the Government of India for outstanding sporting performance, while <b>ICC awards</b> are given by the sport's world governing body.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अंतर्राष्ट्रीय क्रिकेट परिषद (ICC) की महिला माह का सर्वश्रेष्ठ खिलाड़ी</b><br><b>मार्च 2026</b> में भारतीय क्रिकेटर <b>अरुंधति रेड्डी</b> को उनके प्रदर्शन के लिए <b>ICC महिला माह का सर्वश्रेष्ठ खिलाड़ी</b> के रूप में सम्मानित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ICC माह का सर्वश्रेष्ठ खिलाड़ी</b> पुरस्कार <b>जनवरी 2021</b> में आरंभ हुआ और इसका निर्णय एक स्वतंत्र मतदान पैनल करता है।<br>• अरुंधति रेड्डी हैदराबाद की <b>दाहिने हाथ की मध्यम तेज गेंदबाज</b> हैं, जिन्होंने तीनों प्रारूपों में भारत का प्रतिनिधित्व किया है।<br>• वे भारत तथा श्रीलंका द्वारा आयोजित <b>ICC महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप 2025</b> में भारतीय टीम का हिस्सा थीं।<br>• <b>अर्जुन पुरस्कार</b> भारत सरकार उत्कृष्ट खेल प्रदर्शन के लिए देती है, जबकि <b>ICC पुरस्कार</b> खेल की विश्व नियामक संस्था देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073114","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Praveen Kumar Srivastava holds which statutory anti-corruption position in India as of 2026? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2026 तक भारत में प्रवीण कुमार श्रीवास्तव कौन-से सांविधिक भ्रष्टाचार-विरोधी पद पर हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chief Information Commissioner (CIC) of India","hi":"भारत के मुख्य सूचना आयुक्त (CIC)"},"2":{"en":"Central Vigilance Commissioner (CVC) of India","hi":"भारत के केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयुक्त (CVC)"},"3":{"en":"Director of Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI)","hi":"केंद्रीय अन्वेषण ब्यूरो (CBI) के निदेशक"},"4":{"en":"Director of Enforcement in India","hi":"भारत में प्रवर्तन निदेशक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Central Vigilance Commissioner (CVC) of India</b><br><b>Praveen Kumar Srivastava</b> is the <b>Central Vigilance Commissioner</b>, the head of the <b>Central Vigilance Commission</b>, India's apex anti-corruption watchdog.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>CVC</b> was set up in <b>1964</b> on the recommendation of the <b>Santhanam Committee</b> and was given statutory status by the <b>CVC Act, 2003</b>.<br>• The Commission consists of a <b>Central Vigilance Commissioner and not more than two Vigilance Commissioners</b>, appointed by the President on the recommendation of a committee of the Prime Minister, the Home Minister and the Leader of the Opposition in the Lok Sabha.<br>• The CVC is the <b>apex body for vigilance administration</b> in the central government, public sector banks and central public sector undertakings, and it supervises the <b>Delhi Special Police Establishment</b> for vigilance-related cases.<br>• The <b>CIC</b> heads the Central Information Commission under the <b>RTI Act, 2005</b>, while the <b>CBI Director</b> is appointed under the DSPE Act, 1946.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत के केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयुक्त (CVC)</b><br><b>प्रवीण कुमार श्रीवास्तव</b> <b>केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयुक्त</b> हैं, जो भारत की सर्वोच्च भ्रष्टाचार-विरोधी संस्था <b>केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयोग</b> के प्रमुख हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>CVC</b> की स्थापना <b>1964</b> में <b>संथानम समिति</b> की सिफारिश पर हुई तथा इसे <b>CVC अधिनियम, 2003</b> द्वारा सांविधिक दर्जा मिला।<br>• आयोग में <b>एक केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयुक्त तथा दो से अधिक नहीं सतर्कता आयुक्त</b> होते हैं, जिन्हें प्रधानमंत्री, गृह मंत्री तथा लोकसभा में विपक्ष के नेता की समिति की सिफारिश पर राष्ट्रपति नियुक्त करता है।<br>• CVC केंद्र सरकार, सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के बैंकों तथा केंद्रीय सार्वजनिक उपक्रमों में <b>सतर्कता प्रशासन का सर्वोच्च निकाय</b> है और सतर्कता संबंधी मामलों में <b>दिल्ली विशेष पुलिस स्थापना</b> का पर्यवेक्षण करता है।<br>• <b>CIC</b> <b>सूचना का अधिकार अधिनियम, 2005</b> के अंतर्गत केंद्रीय सूचना आयोग का प्रमुख होता है, जबकि <b>CBI निदेशक</b> की नियुक्ति DSPE अधिनियम, 1946 के अंतर्गत होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073115","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"With reference to Earth's biosphere, consider the following statements and choose the <b>correct</b> option:<br>1. Photosynthesis is the primary process responsible for oxygen production.<br>2. Forests are the only natural source of oxygen on Earth.<br>3. Marine ecosystems play a major role in maintaining atmospheric oxygen levels.<br>Which of the statements above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पृथ्वी के जीवमंडल के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार करें तथा <b>सही</b> विकल्प चुनें:<br>1. प्रकाश संश्लेषण ऑक्सीजन उत्पादन के लिए उत्तरदायी प्राथमिक प्रक्रिया है।<br>2. वन पृथ्वी पर ऑक्सीजन के एकमात्र प्राकृतिक स्रोत हैं।<br>3. समुद्री पारितंत्र वायुमंडलीय ऑक्सीजन स्तर बनाए रखने में प्रमुख भूमिका निभाते हैं।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"1 and 3 are correct","hi":"1 तथा 3 सही हैं"},"3":{"en":"2 and 3 are correct","hi":"2 तथा 3 सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"1, 2 and 3 all are correct","hi":"1, 2 तथा 3 सभी सही हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 1 and 3 are correct</b><br>Statement 1 is correct because <b>photosynthesis</b> by green plants, algae and cyanobacteria is the primary source of atmospheric oxygen. Statement 3 is also correct as <b>marine phytoplankton</b> produce a very large share of the oxygen released each year. Statement 2 is wrong because forests are <b>not the only</b> natural source of oxygen.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In photosynthesis, carbon dioxide and water are converted into glucose and oxygen using <b>sunlight, chlorophyll</b> and water, with oxygen released from the splitting of water.<br>• <b>Phytoplankton</b> such as diatoms and cyanobacteria form the base of the marine food web and contribute a large part of global oxygen production.<br>• The <b>biosphere</b> is the zone of life on earth, interacting with the atmosphere, hydrosphere and lithosphere, and its oxygen balance is maintained by the <b>carbon and oxygen cycles</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 1 तथा 3 सही हैं</b><br>कथन 1 सही है क्योंकि हरे पौधों, शैवाल तथा सायनोबैक्टीरिया का <b>प्रकाश संश्लेषण</b> वायुमंडलीय ऑक्सीजन का प्राथमिक स्रोत है। कथन 3 भी सही है क्योंकि <b>समुद्री फाइटोप्लांकटन</b> प्रतिवर्ष मुक्त होने वाली ऑक्सीजन का बहुत बड़ा भाग उत्पन्न करते हैं। कथन 2 गलत है क्योंकि वन ऑक्सीजन के <b>एकमात्र</b> प्राकृतिक स्रोत नहीं हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रकाश संश्लेषण में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड तथा जल <b>सूर्यप्रकाश, क्लोरोफिल</b> तथा जल की सहायता से ग्लूकोज एवं ऑक्सीजन में बदलते हैं, ऑक्सीजन जल के विघटन से मुक्त होती है।<br>• डायटम तथा सायनोबैक्टीरिया जैसे <b>फाइटोप्लांकटन</b> समुद्री खाद्य जाल का आधार हैं तथा वैश्विक ऑक्सीजन उत्पादन का बड़ा भाग देते हैं।<br>• <b>जीवमंडल</b> पृथ्वी पर जीवन का क्षेत्र है, जो वायुमंडल, जलमंडल तथा स्थलमंडल से संपर्क करता है; इसका ऑक्सीजन संतुलन <b>कार्बन एवं ऑक्सीजन चक्र</b> से बना रहता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073116","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Under India's Prime Minister's Overarching Scheme for Holistic Nourishment 2.0 (Poshan) in India initiative, the Supplementary Nutrition Programme has been aligned with which set of programmes as part of the Integrated Nutrition Support Programme? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में प्रधानमंत्री की समग्र पोषण योजना 2.0 (पोषण) पहल के अंतर्गत पूरक पोषण कार्यक्रम को एकीकृत पोषण सहायता कार्यक्रम के भाग के रूप में किन कार्यक्रमों के साथ संरेखित किया गया है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Health Mission (NHM), Ayushman Bharat, Swachh Bharat Mission","hi":"राष्ट्रीय स्वास्थ्य मिशन (NHM), आयुष्मान भारत, स्वच्छ भारत मिशन"},"2":{"en":"Anganwadi Services Scheme, Scheme for Adolescent Girls, POSHAN Abhiyaan","hi":"आंगनबाड़ी सेवा योजना, किशोरी योजना, पोषण अभियान"},"3":{"en":"Mission Indradhanush, Janani Suraksha Yojana, PM Matru Vandana Yojana","hi":"मिशन इंद्रधनुष, जननी सुरक्षा योजना, पीएम मातृ वंदना योजना"},"4":{"en":"Mid-Day Meal Scheme, Skill India Mission, Digital India Programme","hi":"मध्याह्न भोजन योजना, कौशल भारत मिशन, डिजिटल इंडिया कार्यक्रम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Anganwadi Services Scheme, Scheme for Adolescent Girls, POSHAN Abhiyaan</b><br>Under the <b>Mission Poshan 2.0</b> (Prime Minister's Overarching Scheme for Holistic Nourishment), several nutrition schemes were merged, and the <b>Supplementary Nutrition Programme</b> was aligned with the <b>Anganwadi Services Scheme, the Scheme for Adolescent Girls and POSHAN Abhiyaan</b> as part of an <b>Integrated Nutrition Support Programme</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Mission Poshan 2.0</b> is implemented by the <b>Ministry of Women and Child Development</b> and was announced in the Union Budget of 2021-22, taking effect from <b>2021</b>.<br>• It covers children up to 6 years, <b>pregnant women, lactating mothers and adolescent girls</b>, and focuses on maternal nutrition, infant feeding and the prevention of malnutrition.<br>• The Mission promotes <b>home-grown local foods, fortified foods and Ayurvedic nutrition</b>, and uses the <b>Poshan Tracker</b> for real-time monitoring.<br>• It also supports <b>Poshan Vatikas (nutrition gardens)</b> at Anganwadi centres to improve dietary diversity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आंगनबाड़ी सेवा योजना, किशोरी योजना, पोषण अभियान</b><br><b>मिशन पोषण 2.0</b> (प्रधानमंत्री की समग्र पोषण योजना) के अंतर्गत कई पोषण योजनाओं का विलय किया गया तथा <b>पूरक पोषण कार्यक्रम</b> को <b>आंगनबाड़ी सेवा योजना, किशोरी योजना तथा पोषण अभियान</b> के साथ <b>एकीकृत पोषण सहायता कार्यक्रम</b> के रूप में संरेखित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मिशन पोषण 2.0</b> <b>महिला एवं बाल विकास मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा क्रियान्वित होता है और इसकी घोषणा 2021-22 के केंद्रीय बजट में हुई, जो <b>2021</b> से प्रभावी है।<br>• यह 6 वर्ष तक के बच्चों, <b>गर्भवती महिलाओं, स्तनपान कराने वाली माताओं तथा किशोरियों</b> को सम्मिलित करता है और मातृ पोषण, शिशु आहार तथा कुपोषण की रोकथाम पर केंद्रित है।<br>• यह मिशन <b>स्थानीय उत्पादित खाद्य, पोषण-संवर्धित खाद्य तथा आयुर्वेदिक पोषण</b> को बढ़ावा देता है और निगरानी हेतु <b>पोषण ट्रैकर</b> का उपयोग करता है।<br>• यह आहार विविधता बढ़ाने के लिए आंगनबाड़ी केंद्रों पर <b>पोषण वाटिका</b> का भी समर्थन करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073117","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which Maithili memoir won the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी मैथिली संस्मरण-कृति साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त किया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jeete Jee Allahabad","hi":"जीते जी इलाहाबाद"},"2":{"en":"Dhatri Paat San Gaam","hi":"धात्री पात सन गाम"},"3":{"en":"Karhi Khelar Sadhu","hi":"कढ़ी खेलर साधु"},"4":{"en":"Banaras Aa Hum","hi":"बनारस आ हम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Dhatri Paat San Gaam</b><br><b>Dhatri Paat San Gaam</b> is a <b>Maithili memoir</b> that won the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> is given annually for outstanding literary work in each of the languages recognised by the Akademi, and carries a casket, a plaque and a cash prize.<br>• <b>Maithili</b> is an Indo-Aryan language of the <b>Mithila region</b> of Bihar and Nepal and is listed in the <b>Eighth Schedule</b> of the Constitution.<br>• The Sahitya Akademi was founded in <b>1954</b> and is a national academy of letters that also gives the <b>Jnanpith</b> related honours and translation prizes.<br>• Works in Maithili have earlier won Sahitya Akademi awards, and the language has a rich tradition of <b>lyrical poetry and prose</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – धात्री पात सन गाम</b><br><b>धात्री पात सन गाम</b> एक <b>मैथिली संस्मरण</b> है, जिसने <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> प्राप्त किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> प्रत्येक वर्ष अकादमी द्वारा मान्य भाषाओं में उत्कृष्ट साहित्यिक कृति पर दिया जाता है और इसमें पत्रिका, ताम्रपत्र तथा नकद राशि मिलती है।<br>• <b>मैथिली</b> बिहार तथा नेपाल के <b>मिथिला क्षेत्र</b> की भाषा है और संविधान की <b>आठवीं अनुसूची</b> में शामिल है।<br>• साहित्य अकादमी की स्थापना <b>1954</b> में हुई तथा यह राष्ट्रीय साहित्य संस्था है जो अनुवाद पुरस्कार भी देती है।<br>• मैथिली की रचनाओं को पहले भी साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार मिल चुके हैं तथा इस भाषा की <b>गीतात्मक काव्य एवं गद्य</b> की समृद्ध परंपरा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073118","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Rocks, Continents, and Oceans","question":{"en":"Archean rocks contain abundant deposits of all except: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आर्कियन शैलों में निम्नलिखित सभी के प्रचुर भंडार पाए जाते हैं, सिवाय: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manganese","hi":"मैंगनीज"},"2":{"en":"Petroleum","hi":"पेट्रोलियम"},"3":{"en":"Copper","hi":"तांबा"},"4":{"en":"Gold","hi":"सोना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Petroleum</b><br><b>Archean rocks</b> of the Indian shield are rich in metallic minerals such as <b>manganese, copper, gold, iron ore, mica and chromite</b>, but they do <b>not</b> contain petroleum.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Petroleum and coal</b> are found in <b>sedimentary rocks</b> of the Gondwana and Tertiary formations, such as the Mumbai High, Assam and Cambay basins.<br>• Archean rocks are the <b>oldest crystalline rocks</b> of the earth's crust, mostly granites, gneisses and schists, and are called the <b>Aravalli, Dharwar and Singhbhum</b> systems.<br>• <b>Manganese</b> comes mainly from the Dharwar system of Karnataka and the Gondite belt, while <b>copper</b> is mined at <b>Khetri (Rajasthan), Singhbhum (Jharkhand) and Malanjkhand (Madhya Pradesh)</b>.<br>• <b>Gold</b> in India is mined mainly from the <b>Kolar and Hutti</b> gold fields of Karnataka, which lie in Archean rocks.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पेट्रोलियम</b><br>भारतीय शिल्ड की <b>आर्कियन शैलें</b> <b>मैंगनीज, तांबा, सोना, लौह अयस्क, अभ्रक तथा क्रोमाइट</b> जैसे धात्विक खनिजों से समृद्ध हैं, परंतु इनमें <b>पेट्रोलियम नहीं</b> मिलता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पेट्रोलियम तथा कोयला</b> <b>अवसादी शैलों</b> में, गोंडवाना एवं टर्शियरी संरचनाओं में मिलते हैं, जैसे मुंबई हाई, असम तथा कैंबे बेसिन।<br>• आर्कियन शैलें पृथ्वी की पर्पटी की <b>सबसे प्राचीन क्रिस्टलीय शैलें</b> हैं, मुख्यतः ग्रेनाइट, नाइस तथा शिस्ट, जिन्हें <b>अरावली, धारवाड़ तथा सिंहभूम</b> तंत्र कहते हैं।<br>• <b>मैंगनीज</b> मुख्यतः कर्नाटक के धारवाड़ तंत्र तथा गोंडाइट पट्टी से मिलता है, जबकि <b>तांबा</b> <b>खेतड़ी (राजस्थान), सिंहभूम (झारखंड) तथा मलाजखंड (मध्य प्रदेश)</b> से निकाला जाता है।<br>• भारत में <b>सोना</b> मुख्यतः कर्नाटक के <b>कोलार तथा हुट्टी</b> क्षेत्रों से मिलता है, जो आर्कियन शैलों में स्थित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073119","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A attacks Z under grave and sudden provocation, reducing the offence to culpable homicide not amounting to murder. B, who secretly hated Z and was not provoked, joins A and intentionally helps kill Z. What is the correct legal position under Section 3(9) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A गंभीर तथा अचानक उत्तेजना के अंतर्गत Z पर आक्रमण करता है, जिससे अपराध हत्या न होकर सदोष मानव वध बन जाता है। B, जो Z से गुप्त रूप से घृणा करता था और उत्तेजित नहीं था, A के साथ आ मिलता है तथा जानबूझकर Z की हत्या में सहायता करता है। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 की धारा 3(9) के अंतर्गत सही विधिक स्थिति क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both A and B are guilty only of culpable homicide.","hi":"A तथा B दोनों केवल सदोष मानव वध के दोषी हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Both A and B are guilty of murder because they acted together.","hi":"A तथा B दोनों हत्या के दोषी हैं क्योंकि उन्होंने मिलकर कार्य किया।"},"3":{"en":"A is guilty of culpable homicide, while B is guilty of murder.","hi":"A सदोष मानव वध का दोषी है, जबकि B हत्या का दोषी है।"},"4":{"en":"A is innocent due to provocation, while B alone is guilty of murder.","hi":"उत्तेजना के कारण A निर्दोष है, जबकि केवल B हत्या का दोषी है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A is guilty of culpable homicide, while B is guilty of murder</b><br>The benefit of <b>grave and sudden provocation</b> is <b>personal</b> to the person provoked. So <b>A</b> is liable only for <b>culpable homicide not amounting to murder</b>, but <b>B</b>, who was not provoked and joined with the intention to kill, is liable for <b>murder</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Section <b>3(9)</b> of the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> defines the common intention principle; a person is liable for acts done in furtherance of the common intention of all.<br>• Grave and sudden provocation is an exception to murder under the <b>BNS</b> (earlier the Exception to Section 300 of the IPC), reducing the offence to culpable homicide.<br>• Each accused must be judged on his <b>own intention and knowledge</b>, so a private provocation to one accused cannot reduce the liability of a co-participant who was not provoked.<br>• The BNS came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b> and replaced the Indian Penal Code, 1860.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – A सदोष मानव वध का दोषी है, जबकि B हत्या का दोषी है।</b><br><b>गंभीर तथा अचानक उत्तेजना</b> का लाभ केवल <b>उत्तेजित व्यक्ति</b> को व्यक्तिगत रूप से मिलता है। अतः <b>A</b> केवल <b>हत्या न बनने वाले सदोष मानव वध</b> का दोषी है, परंतु <b>B</b>, जो उत्तेजित नहीं था और हत्या के आशय से शामिल हुआ, <b>हत्या</b> का दोषी है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> की धारा <b>3(9)</b> साझा आशय सिद्धांत को परिभाषित करती है; व्यक्ति सभी के साझा आशय की पूर्ति में किए गए कार्यों के लिए उत्तरदायी होता है।<br>• गंभीर तथा अचानक उत्तेजना <b>BNS</b> के अंतर्गत हत्या का अपवाद है (पूर्व में IPC की धारा 300 का अपवाद), जो अपराध को सदोष मानव वध में बदल देता है।<br>• प्रत्येक अभियुक्त का आकलन उसके <b>स्वयं के आशय एवं ज्ञान</b> से होता है, अतः एक अभियुक्त को मिली निजी उत्तेजना उस सहभागी के दायित्व को कम नहीं करती जो उत्तेजित नहीं था।<br>• BNS <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ और इसने भारतीय दंड संहिता, 1860 का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073120","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which environmentalist from Assam is known for creating a forest single-handedly and is popularly referred to as the \"Forest Man of India\"? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"असम के कौन-से पर्यावरणविद् अकेले वन बनाने के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं तथा लोकप्रिय रूप से \"भारत के वन पुरुष\" कहलाते हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jadav Payeng","hi":"जादव पायेंग"},"2":{"en":"Sunderlal Bahuguna","hi":"सुंदरलाल बहुगुणा"},"3":{"en":"Medha Patkar","hi":"मेधा पाटकर"},"4":{"en":"Chandi Prasad Bhatt","hi":"चंडी प्रसाद भट्ट"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Jadav Payeng</b><br><b>Jadav Payeng</b>, known as the <b>Forest Man of India</b>, single-handedly planted trees on a sandbar of the <b>Brahmaputra</b> in Assam over decades, creating the <b>Molai forest</b> near Jorhat.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He began planting in <b>1979</b> on the eroded Majuli island area, and the forest today shelters <b>elephants, tigers, deer and birds</b>.<br>• He was honoured with the <b>Padma Shri in 2015</b> and has been awarded honorary doctorates for his ecological work.<br>• <b>Sunderlal Bahuguna</b> and <b>Chandi Prasad Bhatt</b> were leaders of the <b>Chipko Movement</b> in Uttarakhand, and <b>Medha Patkar</b> is associated with the <b>Narmada Bachao Andolan</b>.<br>• The Molai forest is an example of <b>afforestation and ecological restoration</b> that has reduced soil erosion and improved local biodiversity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जादव पायेंग</b><br><b>भारत के वन पुरुष</b> कहे जाने वाले <b>जादव पायेंग</b> ने असम में <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र</b> के रेतीले भाग पर दशकों तक अकेले पेड़ लगाकर जोरहाट के निकट <b>मोलाई वन</b> बनाया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने <b>1979</b> में माजुली द्वीप के कटाव वाले क्षेत्र में पौधरोपण आरंभ किया और आज यह वन <b>हाथियों, बाघों, हिरणों तथा पक्षियों</b> को आश्रय देता है।<br>• उन्हें <b>2015</b> में <b>पद्म श्री</b> से सम्मानित किया गया तथा उनके पारिस्थितिक कार्य के लिए मानद डॉक्टरेट दी गईं।<br>• <b>सुंदरलाल बहुगुणा</b> तथा <b>चंडी प्रसाद भट्ट</b> उत्तराखंड के <b>चिपको आंदोलन</b> के नेता थे तथा <b>मेधा पाटकर</b> <b>नर्मदा बचाओ आंदोलन</b> से जुड़ी हैं।<br>• मोलाई वन <b>वनरोपण तथा पारिस्थितिक पुनर्स्थापन</b> का उदाहरण है, जिससे मृदा अपरदन घटा और स्थानीय जैव विविधता बढ़ी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073121","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who is the Indian boxer who became the first Indian woman to win six AIBA (Association Internationale de Boxe Amateur) World Boxing Championship titles? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी भारतीय मुक्केबाज छह AIBA (अंतर्राष्ट्रीय शौकिया मुक्केबाजी संघ) विश्व मुक्केबाजी चैंपियनशिप खिताब जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला बनीं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mary Kom","hi":"मैरी कॉम"},"2":{"en":"Lovlina Borgohain","hi":"लवलीना बोरगोहेन"},"3":{"en":"Nikhat Zareen","hi":"निखत ज़रीन"},"4":{"en":"Sarita Devi","hi":"सरिता देवी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mary Kom</b><br><b>M.C. Mary Kom</b> became the first Indian woman to win <b>six AIBA World Boxing Championship</b> titles, a record in women's amateur boxing.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mary Kom, from <b>Manipur</b>, won the world championship title in <b>2002, 2005, 2006, 2008, 2010 and 2018</b>.<br>• She won a <b>bronze medal at the London Olympics 2012</b> in the flyweight category and a gold at the <b>2014 Asian Games</b>.<br>• She was awarded the <b>Padma Vibhushan in 2020</b>, the <b>Padma Bhushan in 2013</b> and the <b>Arjuna Award in 2003</b>, and is a <b>Rajya Sabha</b> member.<br>• <b>Nikhat Zareen</b> is a two-time world champion (2022, 2023) and <b>Lovlina Borgohain</b> won a bronze at the Tokyo Olympics 2020.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मैरी कॉम</b><br><b>एम.सी. मैरी कॉम</b> <b>छह AIBA विश्व मुक्केबाजी चैंपियनशिप</b> खिताब जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला बनीं, जो महिला शौकिया मुक्केबाजी का रिकॉर्ड है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मणिपुर</b> की मैरी कॉम ने विश्व चैंपियनशिप खिताब <b>2002, 2005, 2006, 2008, 2010 तथा 2018</b> में जीते।<br>• उन्होंने <b>लंदन ओलंपिक 2012</b> में फ्लाईवेट वर्ग में <b>कांस्य पदक</b> तथा <b>2014 एशियाई खेलों</b> में स्वर्ण जीता।<br>• उन्हें <b>2020 में पद्म विभूषण</b>, <b>2013 में पद्म भूषण</b> तथा <b>2003 में अर्जुन पुरस्कार</b> मिला और वे <b>राज्यसभा</b> सदस्य भी हैं।<br>• <b>निखत ज़रीन</b> दो बार विश्व चैंपियन (2022, 2023) रही हैं तथा <b>लवलीना बोरगोहेन</b> ने टोक्यो ओलंपिक 2020 में कांस्य पदक जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073122","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which architectural element was successfully minimized in the construction of Gothic cathedrals? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गॉथिक गिरजाघरों के निर्माण में किस स्थापत्य तत्व को सफलतापूर्वक न्यूनतम किया गया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The thick solid walls","hi":"मोटी ठोस दीवारें"},"2":{"en":"The tall glass windows","hi":"लंबी काँच की खिड़कियाँ"},"3":{"en":"The thin stone ribs","hi":"पतली पत्थर की पसलियाँ"},"4":{"en":"The ornate pointed arches","hi":"अलंकृत नुकीले मेहराब"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The thick solid walls</b><br>Gothic architecture reduced <b>thick solid walls</b> by using <b>pointed arches, ribbed vaults and flying buttresses</b>, which carried the load and allowed large windows and tall interiors.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Gothic style developed in <b>northern France</b> in the 12th century and is best seen in <b>Notre-Dame de Paris, Chartres, Reims and Amiens</b> cathedrals.<br>• <b>Flying buttresses</b> transferred the thrust of the roof outwards, so the walls could be thinner and filled with <b>stained glass</b>.<br>• <b>Pointed arches</b> and <b>rib vaults</b> distributed weight more efficiently than the round arches of Romanesque buildings, allowing greater height.<br>• In India, Gothic Revival architecture is seen in <b>Mumbai's Victoria Terminus</b> and the <b>Bombay High Court</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मोटी ठोस दीवारें</b><br>गॉथिक स्थापत्य ने <b>नुकीले मेहराब, पसलीदार मेहराब तथा उड़न पुश्ते (फ्लाइंग बट्रेस)</b> के प्रयोग से <b>मोटी ठोस दीवारों</b> को कम किया, जिससे बड़ी खिड़कियाँ तथा ऊँचा आंतरिक भाग संभव हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गॉथिक शैली 12वीं शताब्दी में <b>उत्तरी फ्रांस</b> में विकसित हुई और <b>नोत्र दाम दे पेरिस, शार्त्र, रेम्स तथा अमियां</b> गिरजाघरों में सर्वोत्तम दिखती है।<br>• <b>उड़न पुश्ते</b> छत का दबाव बाहर स्थानांतरित करते थे, अतः दीवारें पतली होकर <b>रंगीन काँच</b> से भरी जा सकती थीं।<br>• <b>नुकीले मेहराब</b> तथा <b>पसलीदार मेहराब</b> रोमेनेस्क शैली के गोल मेहराबों की तुलना में भार को अधिक कुशलता से बाँटते हैं, जिससे अधिक ऊँचाई संभव होती है।<br>• भारत में गॉथिक पुनरुद्धार स्थापत्य <b>मुंबई के विक्टोरिया टर्मिनस</b> तथा <b>बॉम्बे उच्च न्यायालय</b> में दिखता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073123","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which countries jointly hosted the 2025 Women's Cricket World Cup? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2025 महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप की संयुक्त मेजबानी किन देशों ने की? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India and Sri Lanka","hi":"भारत तथा श्रीलंका"},"2":{"en":"India and Bangladesh","hi":"भारत तथा बांग्लादेश"},"3":{"en":"India and Nepal","hi":"भारत तथा नेपाल"},"4":{"en":"India and Pakistan","hi":"भारत तथा पाकिस्तान"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – India and Sri Lanka</b><br>The <b>ICC Women's Cricket World Cup 2025</b> was jointly hosted by <b>India and Sri Lanka</b>, with the final played in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The tournament was held in <b>September to November 2025</b> and was the <b>10th edition</b> of the Women's Cricket World Cup.<br>• <b>India</b> won the title by defeating <b>South Africa</b> at the <b>DY Patil Stadium, Navi Mumbai</b>, under the captaincy of <b>Harmanpreet Kaur</b>.<br>• The first Women's World Cup was held in <b>1973</b> in England, and <b>Australia</b> is the most successful team in the tournament's history.<br>• The tournament is organised by the <b>International Cricket Council</b> and is played in the <b>One Day International</b> format.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारत तथा श्रीलंका</b><br><b>ICC महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप 2025</b> की संयुक्त मेजबानी <b>भारत तथा श्रीलंका</b> ने की, तथा फाइनल भारत में खेला गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रतियोगिता <b>सितंबर से नवंबर 2025</b> में हुई और महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप का <b>10वाँ संस्करण</b> थी।<br>• <b>भारत</b> ने <b>दक्षिण अफ्रीका</b> को <b>डीवाई पाटिल स्टेडियम, नवी मुंबई</b> में हराकर खिताब जीता, जिसकी कप्तान <b>हरमनप्रीत कौर</b> थीं।<br>• पहला महिला विश्व कप <b>1973</b> में इंग्लैंड में हुआ था तथा इसके इतिहास में <b>ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> सबसे सफल टीम है।<br>• यह प्रतियोगिता <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय क्रिकेट परिषद</b> द्वारा आयोजित होती है और <b>एकदिवसीय अंतर्राष्ट्रीय</b> प्रारूप में खेली जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073124","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which city did the 2025 Men's Hockey Asia Cup, hosted by India, conclude? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत द्वारा आयोजित 2025 पुरुष हॉकी एशिया कप किस शहर में संपन्न हुआ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ranchi","hi":"रांची"},"2":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"},"3":{"en":"Rajgir","hi":"राजगीर"},"4":{"en":"Bhubaneswar","hi":"भुवनेश्वर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rajgir</b><br>The <b>2025 Men's Hockey Asia Cup</b>, hosted by India, was held at the <b>Rajgir Hockey Stadium</b> in <b>Rajgir, Bihar</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The tournament was played in <b>August-September 2025</b>, and <b>India</b> won the title by defeating <b>South Korea</b> in the final.<br>• The Asia Cup is organised by the <b>Asian Hockey Federation</b> and also serves as a qualifier for the <b>Hockey World Cup</b>.<br>• <b>Rajgir</b> is an ancient city of Bihar associated with the <b>Haryanka dynasty</b>, the Buddha and Mahavira, and the stadium there was built for this event.<br>• <b>Bhubaneswar</b> and <b>Rourkela</b> in Odisha host the <b>FIH Pro League</b> and the 2023 Men's World Cup was held at the Kalinga Stadium and Birsa Munda Stadium.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – राजगीर</b><br>भारत द्वारा आयोजित <b>2025 पुरुष हॉकी एशिया कप</b> <b>बिहार</b> के <b>राजगीर</b> स्थित <b>राजगीर हॉकी स्टेडियम</b> में खेला गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रतियोगिता <b>अगस्त-सितंबर 2025</b> में हुई और <b>भारत</b> ने फाइनल में <b>दक्षिण कोरिया</b> को हराकर खिताब जीता।<br>• एशिया कप <b>एशियाई हॉकी महासंघ</b> द्वारा आयोजित होता है तथा <b>हॉकी विश्व कप</b> के लिए क्वालीफायर का कार्य भी करता है।<br>• <b>राजगीर</b> बिहार का प्राचीन नगर है, जो <b>हर्यंक वंश</b>, बुद्ध तथा महावीर से संबंधित है; वहाँ का स्टेडियम इस आयोजन के लिए बनाया गया।<br>• ओडिशा के <b>भुवनेश्वर तथा राउरकेला</b> <b>FIH प्रो लीग</b> की मेजबानी करते हैं तथा 2023 पुरुष विश्व कप कलिंगा स्टेडियम तथा बिरसा मुंडा स्टेडियम में हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073125","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"What does the increased contribution of the service sector after India's 1991 economic reforms primarily indicate? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के 1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद सेवा क्षेत्र के बढ़ते योगदान से मुख्यतः क्या संकेत मिलता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A structural collapse of the agricultural sector","hi":"कृषि क्षेत्र का संरचनात्मक पतन"},"2":{"en":"A structural decline in the industrial sector","hi":"औद्योगिक क्षेत्र में संरचनात्मक गिरावट"},"3":{"en":"A structural reduction in labour productivity","hi":"श्रम उत्पादकता में संरचनात्मक कमी"},"4":{"en":"A structural transformation of the economy","hi":"अर्थव्यवस्था का संरचनात्मक रूपांतरण"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – A structural transformation of the economy</b><br>The rising share of the <b>service sector</b> in GDP after 1991 reflects a <b>structural transformation</b> of the Indian economy from agriculture towards services, driven by liberalisation, technology and trade in services.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Services now contribute over <b>half of India's gross value added</b>, with <b>IT, telecommunications, finance, trade and business services</b> growing fastest.<br>• Structural transformation usually means a shift of output and employment from <b>primary to secondary and tertiary sectors</b>.<br>• In India, the service sector grew rapidly while <b>manufacturing</b> grew more slowly, a pattern sometimes called <b>services-led growth</b>.<br>• Agriculture now provides only about <b>one-sixth of GDP</b> but still supports a large part of the workforce, showing <b>disguised unemployment</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – अर्थव्यवस्था का संरचनात्मक रूपांतरण</b><br>1991 के बाद सकल घरेलू उत्पाद में <b>सेवा क्षेत्र</b> की बढ़ती हिस्सेदारी भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था के कृषि से सेवाओं की ओर <b>संरचनात्मक रूपांतरण</b> को दर्शाती है, जो उदारीकरण, तकनीक तथा सेवा व्यापार से प्रेरित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सेवाएँ अब भारत के <b>सकल मूल्य वर्धन के आधे से अधिक</b> का योगदान देती हैं, जिनमें <b>आईटी, दूरसंचार, वित्त, व्यापार तथा व्यावसायिक सेवाएँ</b> सर्वाधिक तेजी से बढ़ी हैं।<br>• संरचनात्मक रूपांतरण का अर्थ सामान्यतः उत्पादन एवं रोजगार का <b>प्राथमिक से द्वितीयक तथा तृतीयक क्षेत्रों</b> की ओर स्थानांतरण है।<br>• भारत में सेवा क्षेत्र तेजी से बढ़ा जबकि <b>विनिर्माण</b> धीमी गति से बढ़ा, जिसे कभी-कभी <b>सेवा-नेतृत्व वाली वृद्धि</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• कृषि अब सकल घरेलू उत्पाद का लगभग <b>छठा भाग</b> देती है, परंतु श्रमबल का बड़ा भाग इसमें लगा है, जो <b>प्रच्छन्न बेरोजगारी</b> दर्शाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073126","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of the Business Reforms Action Plan (BRAP)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना (BRAP) का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Improve the defence business regulatory environment in States and Union Territories","hi":"राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में रक्षा व्यापार नियामक वातावरण सुधारना"},"2":{"en":"Improve the business regulatory environment in States and Union Territories","hi":"राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में व्यापार नियामक वातावरण सुधारना"},"3":{"en":"Improve the agricultural business regulatory environment in States and Union Territories","hi":"राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में कृषि व्यापार नियामक वातावरण सुधारना"},"4":{"en":"Improve the banking business regulatory environment in States and Union Territories","hi":"राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में बैंकिंग व्यापार नियामक वातावरण सुधारना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Improve the business regulatory environment in States and Union Territories</b><br>The <b>Business Reforms Action Plan (BRAP)</b> ranks States and Union Territories on the reforms they carry out to improve the <b>ease of doing business</b> and the overall <b>business regulatory environment</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRAP was launched by the <b>Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)</b> in <b>2014</b> and assesses States on parameters such as <b>single-window clearance, land availability, labour regulation, online services and dispute resolution</b>.<br>• It is linked to the <b>Ease of Doing Business</b> rankings of the World Bank and encourages <b>competitive federalism</b> among States.<br>• States are graded as <b>Top Achievers, Achievers, Aspirers and Emerging States</b> in the assessment reports.<br>• Related initiatives include <b>Jan Vishwas amendments, the National Single Window System and decriminalisation of minor offences</b> to reduce compliance burden.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों में व्यापार नियामक वातावरण सुधारना</b><br><b>व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना (BRAP)</b> राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों को <b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> तथा समग्र <b>व्यापार नियामक वातावरण</b> सुधारने के लिए किए गए सुधारों पर रैंक करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BRAP को <b>उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग (DPIIT)</b> ने <b>2014</b> में आरंभ किया और यह राज्यों का आकलन <b>एकल खिड़की मंजूरी, भूमि उपलब्धता, श्रम नियमन, ऑनलाइन सेवाएँ तथा विवाद समाधान</b> जैसे मानकों पर करता है।<br>• यह विश्व बैंक की <b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> रैंकिंग से जुड़ी है और राज्यों के बीच <b>प्रतिस्पर्धी संघवाद</b> को प्रोत्साहित करती है।<br>• आकलन रिपोर्टों में राज्यों को <b>शीर्ष उपलब्धिकर्ता, उपलब्धिकर्ता, आकांक्षी तथा उभरते राज्य</b> के रूप में श्रेणीबद्ध किया जाता है।<br>• संबंधित पहलों में अनुपालन बोझ घटाने हेतु <b>जन विश्वास संशोधन, राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली तथा लघु अपराधों का अपराधीकरण हटाना</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073127","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Following the economic reforms introduced in India in 1991, why did many domestic industries face stronger competition in the Indian market? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में 1991 में लाए गए आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद अनेक घरेलू उद्योगों को भारतीय बाजार में अधिक प्रतिस्पर्धा का सामना क्यों करना पड़ा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Due to expansion of public sector manufacturing enterprises","hi":"सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के विनिर्माण उद्यमों के विस्तार के कारण"},"2":{"en":"Due to greater availability of cheaper imported goods","hi":"सस्ते आयातित माल की अधिक उपलब्धता के कारण"},"3":{"en":"Due to increase in industrial licensing requirements","hi":"औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग आवश्यकताओं में वृद्धि के कारण"},"4":{"en":"Due to higher minimum support prices nationwide","hi":"देश भर में उच्च न्यूनतम समर्थन मूल्य के कारण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Due to greater availability of cheaper imported goods</b><br>After 1991, <b>tariffs were cut sharply</b> and quantitative restrictions were removed, so <b>cheaper imported goods</b> entered the Indian market and domestic industries faced stronger competition.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>New Industrial Policy of July 1991</b> abolished industrial licensing for most industries and reduced the role of the public sector.<br>• Peak customs duties fell from over <b>300%</b> in 1990-91 to much lower levels over the following decade, and the rupee was <b>devalued</b> in 1991.<br>• Liberalisation also allowed <b>foreign direct investment</b>, which increased competition and technology inflow.<br>• Competition forced domestic firms to <b>improve quality, cut costs and modernise</b>, while inefficient firms in sectors such as <b>consumer goods and electronics</b> faced pressure.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सस्ते आयातित माल की अधिक उपलब्धता के कारण</b><br>1991 के बाद <b>सीमा शुल्क तेजी से घटाए गए</b> तथा मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंध हटाए गए, अतः <b>सस्ता आयातित माल</b> भारतीय बाजार में आया और घरेलू उद्योगों को अधिक प्रतिस्पर्धा का सामना करना पड़ा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जुलाई 1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> ने अधिकांश उद्योगों की औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की तथा सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र की भूमिका घटाई।<br>• सर्वोच्च सीमा शुल्क 1990-91 के <b>300%</b> से अधिक से अगले दशक में बहुत कम हुआ तथा 1991 में रुपये का <b>अवमूल्यन</b> किया गया।<br>• उदारीकरण ने <b>प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश</b> को भी अनुमति दी, जिससे प्रतिस्पर्धा तथा तकनीकी प्रवाह बढ़ा।<br>• प्रतिस्पर्धा ने घरेलू कंपनियों को <b>गुणवत्ता सुधार, लागत कमी तथा आधुनिकीकरण</b> के लिए विवश किया, जबकि <b>उपभोक्ता वस्तु एवं इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स</b> जैसे क्षेत्रों की अकुशल कंपनियों पर दबाव पड़ा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073128","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Large-scale environmental degradation in modern societies resulted primarily from which of the following? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आधुनिक समाजों में बड़े पैमाने पर पर्यावरणीय क्षरण मुख्यतः निम्नलिखित में से किस कारण हुआ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rejecting all forms of traditional environmental knowledge.","hi":"पारंपरिक पर्यावरणीय ज्ञान के सभी रूपों को अस्वीकार करना।"},"2":{"en":"Using technological innovations that produced no economic benefits.","hi":"ऐसे तकनीकी नवाचारों का उपयोग जिनसे कोई आर्थिक लाभ नहीं हुआ।"},"3":{"en":"Economic growth was pursued without considering ecological consequences.","hi":"पारिस्थितिक परिणामों पर विचार किए बिना आर्थिक विकास को प्राप्त करना।"},"4":{"en":"Establishing wildlife sanctuaries that restricted industrial development.","hi":"वन्यजीव अभयारण्यों की स्थापना जिसने औद्योगिक विकास को सीमित किया।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Economic growth was pursued without considering ecological consequences</b><br>Large-scale environmental degradation in modern societies resulted mainly from the pursuit of <b>economic growth without regard for ecological consequences</b>, through industrialisation, resource extraction and pollution.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Industrial Revolution</b> increased the use of <b>fossil fuels</b>, leading to air pollution, acid rain and greenhouse gas emissions.<br>• Rapid <b>urbanisation, deforestation, intensive agriculture and unregulated mining</b> caused habitat loss, soil erosion and water pollution.<br>• The concept of <b>sustainable development</b>, defined in the <b>Brundtland Report (1987)</b>, seeks to balance growth with environmental protection.<br>• International responses include the <b>Stockholm Conference (1972), Rio Earth Summit (1992), Kyoto Protocol (1997) and Paris Agreement (2015)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पारिस्थितिक परिणामों पर विचार किए बिना आर्थिक विकास को प्राप्त करना।</b><br>आधुनिक समाजों में बड़े पैमाने पर पर्यावरणीय क्षरण मुख्यतः <b>पारिस्थितिक परिणामों की परवाह किए बिना आर्थिक विकास</b> को प्राप्त करने से हुआ - औद्योगीकरण, संसाधन निष्कर्षण तथा प्रदूषण के माध्यम से।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>औद्योगिक क्रांति</b> ने <b>जीवाश्म ईंधन</b> का उपयोग बढ़ाया, जिससे वायु प्रदूषण, अम्लीय वर्षा तथा ग्रीनहाउस गैस उत्सर्जन बढ़ा।<br>• तेज <b>शहरीकरण, वनों की कटाई, सघन कृषि तथा अनियंत्रित खनन</b> से आवास क्षति, मृदा अपरदन तथा जल प्रदूषण हुआ।<br>• <b>ब्रुंटलैंड रिपोर्ट (1987)</b> में परिभाषित <b>सतत विकास</b> की संकल्पना विकास तथा पर्यावरण संरक्षण में संतुलन खोजती है।<br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रतिक्रियाओं में <b>स्टॉकहोम सम्मेलन (1972), रियो पृथ्वी शिखर सम्मेलन (1992), क्योटो प्रोटोकॉल (1997) तथा पेरिस समझौता (2015)</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073129","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Which of the following conclusions can be inferred from India's traditional practices of respecting and conserving nature? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रकृति का सम्मान तथा संरक्षण करने की भारत की पारंपरिक प्रथाओं से निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Conservation in India is solely the responsibility of governments.","hi":"भारत में संरक्षण पूर्णतः सरकारों की जिम्मेदारी है।"},"2":{"en":"Human survival in India is independent of ecosystem functioning.","hi":"भारत में मानव अस्तित्व पारितंत्र कार्यप्रणाली से स्वतंत्र है।"},"3":{"en":"Environmental ethics are deeply rooted in Indian traditions.","hi":"पर्यावरणीय नैतिकता भारतीय परंपराओं में गहराई से निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Urbanisation in India completely disconnects people from nature.","hi":"भारत में शहरीकरण लोगों को प्रकृति से पूर्णतः अलग कर देता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Environmental ethics are deeply rooted in Indian traditions</b><br>India's traditional practices of <b>worshipping trees, rivers and animals</b>, such as the sacred groves, the tulsi plant and the peepal tree, show that <b>environmental ethics are deeply rooted in Indian traditions</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sacred groves (sarna, devrai, orans)</b> are patches of forest protected by local communities on religious grounds and preserve rich biodiversity.<br>• <b>Ahimsa, Bishnoi traditions, Chipko and Appiko movements</b> and festivals such as <b>van mahotsav</b> reflect a tradition of conservation.<br>• The <b>Bishnoi community of Rajasthan</b> is known for protecting the khejri tree and blackbuck, inspiring the <b>Khejarli sacrifice of 1730</b>.<br>• The Constitution also reflects these values through <b>Article 48A (DPSP)</b> and <b>Article 51A(g)</b>, which make environmental protection a duty of the State and of citizens.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पर्यावरणीय नैतिकता भारतीय परंपराओं में गहराई से निहित है।</b><br>पेड़, नदियों तथा पशुओं की पूजा जैसी भारत की पारंपरिक प्रथाएँ, जैसे पवित्र उपवन, तुलसी तथा पीपल का वृक्ष, दर्शाती हैं कि <b>पर्यावरणीय नैतिकता भारतीय परंपराओं में गहराई से निहित है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पवित्र उपवन (सरना, देवराई, ओरण)</b> वनों के वे भाग हैं जिन्हें स्थानीय समुदाय धार्मिक आधार पर संरक्षित रखते हैं और जहाँ समृद्ध जैव विविधता पाई जाती है।<br>• <b>अहिंसा, बिश्नोई परंपरा, चिपको तथा अप्पिको आंदोलन</b> एवं <b>वन महोत्सव</b> जैसे उत्सव संरक्षण की परंपरा दर्शाते हैं।<br>• <b>राजस्थान का बिश्नोई समुदाय</b> खेजड़ी वृक्ष तथा काला हिरण की रक्षा के लिए जाना जाता है, जिसने <b>1730 के खेजड़ली बलिदान</b> को प्रेरित किया।<br>• संविधान भी इन मूल्यों को <b>अनुच्छेद 48A (नीति निदेशक तत्व)</b> तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 51A(g)</b> के माध्यम से दर्शाता है, जो पर्यावरण संरक्षण को राज्य तथा नागरिकों का कर्तव्य बनाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073130","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following factors would increase the demand for laptops and shift their demand curve to the right? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कारक लैपटॉप की माँग बढ़ाएगा तथा उसकी माँग वक्र को दाईं ओर खिसकाएगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An increase in the price of laptops","hi":"लैपटॉप के मूल्य में वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"A decrease in consumer income, assuming laptops are normal goods","hi":"उपभोक्ता आय में कमी, यह मानते हुए कि लैपटॉप सामान्य वस्तुएँ हैं"},"3":{"en":"An increase in the price of internet services used with laptops","hi":"लैपटॉप के साथ प्रयुक्त इंटरनेट सेवाओं के मूल्य में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"An increase in consumers' preference for online education","hi":"ऑनलाइन शिक्षा के प्रति उपभोक्ताओं की वरीयता में वृद्धि"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – An increase in consumers' preference for online education</b><br>A rise in <b>consumers' preference</b> for online education makes laptops more desirable at every price, so the <b>demand curve shifts to the right</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A change in the <b>price of the good itself</b> causes a <b>movement along</b> the demand curve, not a shift, so option 1 is wrong.<br>• For a <b>normal good</b>, a fall in income reduces demand and shifts the curve to the left, so option 2 is wrong.<br>• Laptops and internet services are <b>complements</b>; a rise in the price of internet services reduces laptop demand, so option 3 is wrong.<br>• Other factors that shift demand to the right are a rise in <b>income, population, price of substitutes</b> and favourable <b>tastes and expectations</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ऑनलाइन शिक्षा के प्रति उपभोक्ताओं की वरीयता में वृद्धि</b><br>ऑनलाइन शिक्षा के प्रति <b>उपभोक्ताओं की वरीयता</b> बढ़ने से हर मूल्य पर लैपटॉप अधिक वांछनीय हो जाता है, अतः <b>माँग वक्र दाईं ओर खिसक जाता है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>स्वयं वस्तु के मूल्य</b> में परिवर्तन से माँग वक्र पर <b>गति</b> होती है, वक्र नहीं खिसकता, अतः विकल्प 1 गलत है।<br>• <b>सामान्य वस्तु</b> के लिए आय घटने पर माँग घटती है और वक्र बाईं ओर खिसकता है, अतः विकल्प 2 गलत है।<br>• लैपटॉप तथा इंटरनेट सेवाएँ <b>पूरक वस्तुएँ</b> हैं; इंटरनेट सेवाओं के मूल्य में वृद्धि से लैपटॉप की माँग घटती है, अतः विकल्प 3 गलत है।<br>• माँग वक्र को दाईं ओर खिसकाने वाले अन्य कारक <b>आय, जनसंख्या, स्थानापन्न वस्तुओं के मूल्य</b> में वृद्धि तथा अनुकूल <b>रुचि एवं अपेक्षाएँ</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073131","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What are the x-axis values (class midpoints) used to plot the frequency polygon?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर देने के लिए नीचे दिए गए बारंबारता बहुभुज का निरीक्षण कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>बारंबारता बहुभुज बनाने के लिए प्रयुक्त x-अक्ष के मान (वर्ग मध्यबिंदु) क्या हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0, 50, 100, 150, 200"},"2":{"en":"25, 75, 125, 175, 225"},"3":{"en":"50, 100, 150, 200, 250"},"4":{"en":"10, 30, 50, 70, 90"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The classes marked on the axis are 0–50, 50–100, 100–150, 150–200, 200–250<br>Midpoint of a class = \\(\\frac{\\text{lower} + \\text{upper}}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{0+50}{2}=25,\\ \\frac{50+100}{2}=75,\\ \\frac{100+150}{2}=125,\\ \\frac{150+200}{2}=175,\\ \\frac{200+250}{2}=225\\)<br>Midpoints = \\(\\boxed{25, 75, 125, 175, 225}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25, 75, 125, 175, 225.</b>","hi":"अक्ष पर अंकित वर्ग 0–50, 50–100, 100–150, 150–200, 200–250 हैं<br>वर्ग का मध्यबिंदु = \\(\\frac{\\text{निचली} + \\text{ऊपरी}}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{0+50}{2}=25,\\ \\frac{50+100}{2}=75,\\ \\frac{100+150}{2}=125,\\ \\frac{150+200}{2}=175,\\ \\frac{200+250}{2}=225\\)<br>मध्यबिंदु = \\(\\boxed{25, 75, 125, 175, 225}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25, 75, 125, 175, 225 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg"]}},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073132","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Convert π radians to degrees. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"π रेडियन को डिग्री में बदलिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180º"},"2":{"en":"90º"},"3":{"en":"360º"},"4":{"en":"270º"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\pi\\) radians = \\(180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\pi \\times \\frac{180}{\\pi} = \\boxed{180^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 180º.</b>","hi":"\\(\\pi\\) रेडियन = \\(180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\pi \\times \\frac{180}{\\pi} = \\boxed{180^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 180º है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073133","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Examine the bar graph below to , answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q53.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which city has the lowest average value across all three zones?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q53.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए गए बार ग्राफ का निरीक्षण कीजिए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q53.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>किस शहर का तीनों ज़ोन में औसत मान सबसे कम है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q53.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"},"2":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"},"3":{"en":"Kolkata","hi":"कोलकाता"},"4":{"en":"Lucknow","hi":"लखनऊ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the graph the three bars of each city are close together, so the average follows the height of the bars.<br>Delhi ≈ 317, Mumbai ≈ 211, Kolkata ≈ 279, Chennai ≈ 240, Lucknow ≈ 308<br>Lowest average = \\(\\boxed{\\text{Mumbai}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Mumbai.</b>","hi":"ग्राफ में प्रत्येक शहर के तीनों स्तंभ निकट-निकट हैं, अतः औसत स्तंभों की ऊँचाई के अनुसार ही होगा।<br>दिल्ली ≈ 317, मुंबई ≈ 211, कोलकाता ≈ 279, चेन्नई ≈ 240, लखनऊ ≈ 308<br>सबसे कम औसत = \\(\\boxed{\\text{मुंबई}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): मुंबई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q53.jpg"]}},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073134","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of a number is 72, then what is \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of that same number? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी संख्या का \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) भाग 72 है, तो उसी संख्या का \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) भाग क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"54"},"2":{"en":"64"},"3":{"en":"74"},"4":{"en":"84"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of the number = 72 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) number = \\(72 \\times \\frac{4}{3} = 96\\)<br>Required value = \\(96 \\times \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{64}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 64.</b>","hi":"संख्या का \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) भाग = 72 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) संख्या = \\(72 \\times \\frac{4}{3} = 96\\)<br>अभीष्ट मान = \\(96 \\times \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{64}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 64 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073135","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Ramesh travels from his home to college at 40 km/h and arrives 25 minutes late. On the following day, he increases his speed to 50 km/h but is still 10 minutes late. Find the distance between his home and college. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रमेश अपने घर से कॉलेज 40 km/h की चाल से जाता है और 25 मिनट देर से पहुँचता है। अगले दिन वह अपनी चाल 50 km/h कर लेता है, फिर भी 10 मिनट देर से पहुँचता है। उसके घर और कॉलेज के बीच की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30 km"},"2":{"en":"40 km"},"3":{"en":"50 km"},"4":{"en":"60 km"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Difference of delays = \\(25 - 10 = 15\\) minutes = \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) h<br>\\(\\frac{d}{40} - \\frac{d}{50} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5d - 4d}{200} = \\frac{1}{4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{d}{200} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{50}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 50 km.</b>","hi":"देरी का अंतर = \\(25 - 10 = 15\\) मिनट = \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) घंटे<br>\\(\\frac{d}{40} - \\frac{d}{50} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5d - 4d}{200} = \\frac{1}{4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{d}{200} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{50}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 50 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073136","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(0.87)^3 - (0.13)^3}{(0.87)^2 + 0.1131 + (0.13)^2}\\). [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(0.87)^3 - (0.13)^3}{(0.87)^2 + 0.1131 + (0.13)^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.48"},"2":{"en":"0.56"},"3":{"en":"0.24"},"4":{"en":"0.74"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Here \\(a = 0.87\\), \\(b = 0.13\\) and \\(ab = 0.87 \\times 0.13 = 0.1131\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.87 - 0.13 = \\boxed{0.74}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.74.</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(a = 0.87\\), \\(b = 0.13\\) और \\(ab = 0.87 \\times 0.13 = 0.1131\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.87 - 0.13 = \\boxed{0.74}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0.74 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073137","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If a 6-digit number 4x57y2 is divisible by 72, then what is the value of (x + y)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 6 अंकों की संख्या 4x57y2, 72 से विभाज्य है, तो (x + y) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"9"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"72 = 8 × 9. For divisibility by 8, the last three digits 7y2 must be divisible by 8<br>\\(712 = 8 \\times 89\\) \\(\\Rightarrow y = 1\\)<br>For divisibility by 9, digit sum \\(= 4 + x + 5 + 7 + 1 + 2 = 19 + x\\) must be a multiple of 9 \\(\\Rightarrow x = 8\\)<br>\\(x + y = 8 + 1 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 9.</b>","hi":"72 = 8 × 9. 8 से विभाज्यता के लिए अंतिम तीन अंक 7y2, 8 से विभाज्य होने चाहिए<br>\\(712 = 8 \\times 89\\) \\(\\Rightarrow y = 1\\)<br>9 से विभाज्यता के लिए अंकों का योग \\(= 4 + x + 5 + 7 + 1 + 2 = 19 + x\\), 9 का गुणज होना चाहिए \\(\\Rightarrow x = 8\\)<br>\\(x + y = 8 + 1 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073138","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A, B, and C started a business with capital in the ratio 2:3:5. At the end of 4 months, A increases his capital by 50%, and B decreases his capital by \\(33\\frac{1}{3}\\)%. Find the profit ratio at the end of the year. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A, B और C ने 2:3:5 के अनुपात में पूँजी लगाकर एक व्यवसाय शुरू किया। 4 महीने के अंत में A अपनी पूँजी 50% बढ़ा देता है और B अपनी पूँजी \\(33\\frac{1}{3}\\)% घटा देता है। वर्ष के अंत में लाभ का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11 : 13 : 20"},"2":{"en":"14 : 13 : 30"},"3":{"en":"8 : 7 : 15"},"4":{"en":"8 : 9 : 15"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Capitals: A = 2, B = 3, C = 5 (per unit share)<br>After 4 months A becomes 3 and B becomes 2<br>A's capital-days = \\(2 \\times 4 + 3 \\times 8 = 8 + 24 = 32\\)<br>B's capital-days = \\(3 \\times 4 + 2 \\times 8 = 12 + 16 = 28\\)<br>C's capital-days = \\(5 \\times 12 = 60\\)<br>Profit ratio = \\(32 : 28 : 60 = \\boxed{8 : 7 : 15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8 : 7 : 15.</b>","hi":"पूँजियाँ: A = 2, B = 3, C = 5 (प्रति इकाई हिस्सा)<br>4 महीने बाद A की 3 और B की 2 हो जाती है<br>A की पूँजी-महीने = \\(2 \\times 4 + 3 \\times 8 = 8 + 24 = 32\\)<br>B की पूँजी-महीने = \\(3 \\times 4 + 2 \\times 8 = 12 + 16 = 28\\)<br>C की पूँजी-महीने = \\(5 \\times 12 = 60\\)<br>लाभ अनुपात = \\(32 : 28 : 60 = \\boxed{8 : 7 : 15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 : 7 : 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073139","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"Given that the average of five numbers is 27, and that excluding one number results in an average of 25 for the remaining four numbers, determine the value of the excluded number. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यह दिया गया है कि पाँच संख्याओं का औसत 27 है और एक संख्या को छोड़ने पर शेष चार संख्याओं का औसत 25 हो जाता है, तो छोड़ी गई संख्या का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45"},"2":{"en":"35"},"3":{"en":"55"},"4":{"en":"75"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Sum of five numbers = \\(27 \\times 5 = 135\\)<br>Sum of the remaining four = \\(25 \\times 4 = 100\\)<br>Excluded number = \\(135 - 100 = \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 35.</b>","hi":"पाँच संख्याओं का योग = \\(27 \\times 5 = 135\\)<br>शेष चार संख्याओं का योग = \\(25 \\times 4 = 100\\)<br>छोड़ी गई संख्या = \\(135 - 100 = \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073140","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"Determine the area of the region formed by the graph of the equation y=|x−1| and the line y=3. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"समीकरण y=|x−1| के ग्राफ और रेखा y=3 से बनने वाले क्षेत्र का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 sq. units"},"2":{"en":"12 sq. units"},"3":{"en":"9 sq. units"},"4":{"en":"18 sq. units"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M10 145H222\"/><path d=\"M78 30V160\"/><path d=\"M8 82H226\"/><path d=\"M18 82L108 145L198 82\"/><path d=\"M108 145V82\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"108\" cy=\"145\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"82\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"198\" cy=\"82\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">y = 3</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">y = 3</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">|x – 1|</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">|x – 1|</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">3</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">3</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(1, 0)</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">(1, 0)</text></g></svg><br>\\(|x - 1| = 3 \\Rightarrow x = 4\\) or \\(x = -2\\)<br>Base on the line \\(y = 3\\) = \\(4 - (-2) = 6\\) units, height = 3 units<br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 3 = \\boxed{9}\\) sq. units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 9 sq. units.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M10 145H222\"/><path d=\"M78 30V160\"/><path d=\"M8 82H226\"/><path d=\"M18 82L108 145L198 82\"/><path d=\"M108 145V82\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"108\" cy=\"145\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"82\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"198\" cy=\"82\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">y = 3</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">y = 3</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">|x – 1|</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">|x – 1|</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">3</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">3</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(1, 0)</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">(1, 0)</text></g></svg><br>\\(|x - 1| = 3 \\Rightarrow x = 4\\) या \\(x = -2\\)<br>रेखा \\(y = 3\\) पर आधार = \\(4 - (-2) = 6\\) इकाई, ऊँचाई = 3 इकाई<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 3 = \\boxed{9}\\) वर्ग इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 9 sq. units है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073141","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If a cube has a diagonal of \\(18\\sqrt{3}\\) cm and is melted to form a cuboid, its length is equal to the side of the cube, and its breadth is 9 cm. Find the height of the cuboid. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी घन का विकर्ण \\(18\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है और उसे पिघलाकर एक घनाभ बनाया जाता है, जिसकी लंबाई घन की भुजा के बराबर है और चौड़ाई 9 cm है। घनाभ की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"44 cm"},"2":{"en":"27 cm"},"3":{"en":"36 cm"},"4":{"en":"49 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"330\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M30 40H110V120H30Z\"/><path d=\"M68 14H148V94H68Z\"/><path d=\"M30 40L68 14M110 40L148 14M110 120L148 94\"/><path d=\"M30 120L148 14\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M165 70H185M181 64L187 70L181 76\"/><path d=\"M210 50H248V130H210Z\"/><path d=\"M228 38H266V118H228Z\"/><path d=\"M210 50L228 38M248 50L266 38M248 130L266 118\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18√3</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18√3</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">9</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">9</text><text x=\"203\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"203\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"273\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"273\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text></g></svg><br>Diagonal of a cube = \\(a\\sqrt{3} = 18\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 18\\) cm<br>Volume of the cube = \\(18^3 = 5832\\) cm³<br>For the cuboid, \\(18 \\times 9 \\times h = 5832\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{5832}{162} = \\boxed{36}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 36 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"330\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M30 40H110V120H30Z\"/><path d=\"M68 14H148V94H68Z\"/><path d=\"M30 40L68 14M110 40L148 14M110 120L148 94\"/><path d=\"M30 120L148 14\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M165 70H185M181 64L187 70L181 76\"/><path d=\"M210 50H248V130H210Z\"/><path d=\"M228 38H266V118H228Z\"/><path d=\"M210 50L228 38M248 50L266 38M248 130L266 118\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18√3</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18√3</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">9</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">9</text><text x=\"203\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"203\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"273\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"273\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text></g></svg><br>घन का विकर्ण = \\(a\\sqrt{3} = 18\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 18\\) cm<br>घन का आयतन = \\(18^3 = 5832\\) cm³<br>घनाभ के लिए, \\(18 \\times 9 \\times h = 5832\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{5832}{162} = \\boxed{36}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 36 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073142","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosec θ + cot θ = \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\), find the value of tan θ. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि cosec θ + cot θ = \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) है, तो tan θ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{20}{21}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{21}{20}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\cot\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{5}{2}\\)<br>So \\(\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{2\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{1 - \\tan^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{4}{5}}{1 - \\frac{4}{25}}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\frac{4}{5}}{\\frac{21}{25}} = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{21}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{20}{21}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\cot\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{5}{2}\\)<br>अतः \\(\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{2\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{1 - \\tan^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{4}{5}}{1 - \\frac{4}{25}}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\frac{4}{5}}{\\frac{21}{25}} = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{21}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{20}{21}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073143","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} - 3}}\\), then what is the value of \\(X^2 + \\frac{1}{X^2}\\)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} - 3}}\\) है, तो \\(X^2 + \\frac{1}{X^2}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"32"},"4":{"en":"38"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(X^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} - 3} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} + 3} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{10} + 3)^2}{10 - 9}\\)<br>\\(= 19 + 6\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{X^2} = 19 - 6\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>\\(X^2 + \\frac{1}{X^2} = 19 + 6\\sqrt{10} + 19 - 6\\sqrt{10} = \\boxed{38}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 38.</b>","hi":"\\(X^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} - 3} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{10} + 3}{\\sqrt{10} + 3} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{10} + 3)^2}{10 - 9}\\)<br>\\(= 19 + 6\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{X^2} = 19 - 6\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>\\(X^2 + \\frac{1}{X^2} = 19 + 6\\sqrt{10} + 19 - 6\\sqrt{10} = \\boxed{38}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 38 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073144","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Triangles ΔABC and ΔPQR satisfy the conditions AB = PQ and ∠B = ∠Q. Under what additional condition can we conclude that ΔABC ≅ ΔPQR by the SAS congruence criterion? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ΔABC और ΔPQR शर्तों AB = PQ और ∠B = ∠Q को संतुष्ट करते हैं। किस अतिरिक्त शर्त के अंतर्गत हम निष्कर्ष निकाल सकते हैं कि SAS सर्वांगसमता कसौटी से ΔABC ≅ ΔPQR है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BC = QR"},"2":{"en":"AC = PR"},"3":{"en":"AC = QR"},"4":{"en":"BC = PQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 150\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 32L28 115H120Z\"/><path d=\"M200 32L168 115H260Z\"/><path d=\"M44 68L40 60\"/><path d=\"M184 68L180 60\"/><path d=\"M42 115A15 15 0 0 0 34 103\"/><path d=\"M182 115A15 15 0 0 0 174 103\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"264\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R</text><text x=\"264\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">BC = ?</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">BC = ?</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">QR = ?</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">QR = ?</text></g></svg><br>In SAS, the equal angle must lie between the two pairs of equal sides<br>Sides forming ∠B are AB and BC; sides forming ∠Q are PQ and QR<br>AB = PQ is given, so the third condition needed is \\(\\boxed{BC = QR}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): BC = QR.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 150\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 32L28 115H120Z\"/><path d=\"M200 32L168 115H260Z\"/><path d=\"M44 68L40 60\"/><path d=\"M184 68L180 60\"/><path d=\"M42 115A15 15 0 0 0 34 103\"/><path d=\"M182 115A15 15 0 0 0 174 103\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"264\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R</text><text x=\"264\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">BC = ?</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">BC = ?</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">QR = ?</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">QR = ?</text></g></svg><br>SAS में बराबर कोण दोनों बराबर भुजाओं के बीच होना चाहिए<br>∠B बनाने वाली भुजाएँ AB और BC हैं; ∠Q बनाने वाली भुजाएँ PQ और QR हैं<br>AB = PQ दिया है, अतः तीसरी आवश्यक शर्त \\(\\boxed{BC = QR}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): BC = QR है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073145","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A gold biscuit weighing 11 kg contained only 82% gold and the rest copper. If it was alloyed with another gold biscuit and the resulting alloy had a mass of 28 kg and contained 90% gold, then find the approximate percentage of gold in the second biscuit? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"11 kg वजन के एक सोने के बिस्किट में केवल 82% सोना और शेष ताँबा था। यदि इसे दूसरे सोने के बिस्किट के साथ मिलाया गया और परिणामी मिश्रातु का द्रव्यमान 28 kg तथा उसमें 90% सोना था, तो दूसरे बिस्किट में सोने का अनुमानित प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"90.5%"},"2":{"en":"92.7%"},"3":{"en":"94.8%"},"4":{"en":"95.2%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"First biscuit: gold = \\(11 \\times \\frac{82}{100} = 9.02\\) kg<br>Alloy: gold = \\(28 \\times \\frac{90}{100} = 25.2\\) kg<br>Second biscuit: mass = \\(28 - 11 = 17\\) kg, gold = \\(25.2 - 9.02 = 16.18\\) kg<br>Percentage = \\(\\frac{16.18}{17} \\times 100 = 95.18 \\approx \\boxed{95.2}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 95.2%.</b>","hi":"पहला बिस्किट: सोना = \\(11 \\times \\frac{82}{100} = 9.02\\) kg<br>मिश्रातु: सोना = \\(28 \\times \\frac{90}{100} = 25.2\\) kg<br>दूसरा बिस्किट: द्रव्यमान = \\(28 - 11 = 17\\) kg, सोना = \\(25.2 - 9.02 = 16.18\\) kg<br>प्रतिशत = \\(\\frac{16.18}{17} \\times 100 = 95.18 \\approx \\boxed{95.2}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 95.2% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073146","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of the annual budget allocation across various departments. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on it.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the company decides to double the budget for 'Research &amp; Development' by reducing the budget for 'Miscellaneous' and 'Infrastructure' equally, what will be the new percentage share of 'Miscellaneous' in the budget?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट विभिन्न विभागों में वार्षिक बजट आवंटन का प्रतिशत-वार वितरण दर्शाता है। पाई-चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए और उसके आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि कंपनी 'मिसेलेनियस' और 'इन्फ्रास्ट्रक्चर' का बजट समान रूप से घटाकर 'रिसर्च एंड डेवलपमेंट' का बजट दोगुना करने का निर्णय लेती है, तो बजट में 'मिसेलेनियस' की नई प्रतिशत हिस्सेदारी क्या होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0%"},"2":{"en":"5%"},"3":{"en":"2.5%"},"4":{"en":"4.5%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the pie-chart: Salaries 25%, Marketing 25%, Research &amp; Development 20%, Infrastructure 20%, Miscellaneous 10%<br>Extra budget needed for R&amp;D = 20%<br>Reduction from Miscellaneous + Infrastructure = 20%, equally = 10% each<br>New Miscellaneous share = \\(10 - 10 = \\boxed{0}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0%.</b>","hi":"पाई-चार्ट से: सैलरीज़ 25%, मार्केटिंग 25%, रिसर्च एंड डेवलपमेंट 20%, इन्फ्रास्ट्रक्चर 20%, मिसेलेनियस 10%<br>R&amp;D के लिए अतिरिक्त बजट = 20%<br>मिसेलेनियस + इन्फ्रास्ट्रक्चर से कटौती = 20%, समान रूप से = प्रत्येक 10%<br>मिसेलेनियस की नई हिस्सेदारी = \\(10 - 10 = \\boxed{0}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q66.jpg"]}},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073147","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"An engineer splits an investment of ₹6,00,000 into two equal parts. The first part is invested at an annual simple interest rate of 8%, and the second part is invested at an annual simple interest rate of 11%. If both parts are invested for a duration of 5 years, calculate the total simple interest earned from both investments combined. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक इंजीनियर ₹6,00,000 का निवेश दो समान भागों में बाँटता है। पहला भाग 8% वार्षिक साधारण ब्याज दर पर और दूसरा भाग 11% वार्षिक साधारण ब्याज दर पर निवेश किया जाता है। यदि दोनों भाग 5 वर्ष की अवधि के लिए निवेश किए जाते हैं, तो दोनों निवेशों से मिलाकर अर्जित कुल साधारण ब्याज की गणना कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,00,000"},"2":{"en":"₹2,25,000"},"3":{"en":"₹2,22,000"},"4":{"en":"₹2,85,000"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each part = ₹3,00,000<br>Interest on the first part = \\(\\frac{300000 \\times 8 \\times 5}{100} = 120000\\)<br>Interest on the second part = \\(\\frac{300000 \\times 11 \\times 5}{100} = 165000\\)<br>Total interest = \\(120000 + 165000 = \\boxed{285000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹2,85,000.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक भाग = ₹3,00,000<br>पहले भाग पर ब्याज = \\(\\frac{300000 \\times 8 \\times 5}{100} = 120000\\)<br>दूसरे भाग पर ब्याज = \\(\\frac{300000 \\times 11 \\times 5}{100} = 165000\\)<br>कुल ब्याज = \\(120000 + 165000 = \\boxed{285000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹2,85,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073148","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosA = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) and sinB = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), where A and B are acute angles, then find the value of A – B. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि cosA = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) और sinB = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) है, जहाँ A और B न्यून कोण हैं, तो A – B का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos A = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow A = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow B = 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(A - B = 60^\\circ - 30^\\circ = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos A = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow A = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow B = 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(A - B = 60^\\circ - 30^\\circ = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073149","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A team of 15 volunteers can plant a plot of saplings in 8 hours. On the day of the project, 5 volunteers do not show up. Assuming all volunteers work at the same pace, how long will it take the remaining team to complete the planting? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"15 स्वयंसेवकों की एक टीम पौधे लगाने के एक भूखंड को 8 घंटे में पूरा कर सकती है। परियोजना के दिन 5 स्वयंसेवक नहीं आते। यह मानते हुए कि सभी स्वयंसेवक समान गति से कार्य करते हैं, शेष टीम को पौधे लगाने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 hrs"},"2":{"en":"11.5 hrs"},"3":{"en":"10 hrs"},"4":{"en":"9.6 hrs"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Work = \\(15 \\times 8 = 120\\) volunteer-hours<br>Remaining volunteers = \\(15 - 5 = 10\\)<br>Time = \\(\\frac{120}{10} = \\boxed{12}\\) hrs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 12 hrs.</b>","hi":"कार्य = \\(15 \\times 8 = 120\\) स्वयंसेवक-घंटे<br>शेष स्वयंसेवक = \\(15 - 5 = 10\\)<br>समय = \\(\\frac{120}{10} = \\boxed{12}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 12 hrs है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073150","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tan A = cot B and cos A = sin(90º–2B) for acute angles, find A and B. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि न्यून कोणों के लिए tan A = cot B और cos A = sin(90º–2B) है, तो A और B ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A=30º, B=60º"},"2":{"en":"A=60º, B=30º"},"3":{"en":"A=45º, B=45º"},"4":{"en":"A=50º, B=40º"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan A = \\cot B = \\tan(90^\\circ - B) \\Rightarrow A + B = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos A = \\sin(90^\\circ - 2B) = \\cos 2B \\Rightarrow A = 2B\\)<br>\\(2B + B = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow B = 30^\\circ,\\ A = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{A = 60^\\circ,\\ B = 30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A=60º, B=30º.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan A = \\cot B = \\tan(90^\\circ - B) \\Rightarrow A + B = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos A = \\sin(90^\\circ - 2B) = \\cos 2B \\Rightarrow A = 2B\\)<br>\\(2B + B = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow B = 30^\\circ,\\ A = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{A = 60^\\circ,\\ B = 30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): A=60º, B=30º है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073151","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If p + q + r = 24 and pq + qr + rp = 65, then find the value of p² + q² + r². [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि p + q + r = 24 और pq + qr + rp = 65 है, तो p² + q² + r² का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"412"},"2":{"en":"446"},"3":{"en":"486"},"4":{"en":"526"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = (p + q + r)^2 - 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(= 24^2 - 2 \\times 65 = 576 - 130\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{446}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 446.</b>","hi":"\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = (p + q + r)^2 - 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(= 24^2 - 2 \\times 65 = 576 - 130\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{446}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 446 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073152","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Which of the following is true? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सत्य है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt[4]{10} \\gt \\sqrt[3]{6}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{6} \\gt \\sqrt[4]{10}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{6}\\) and \\(\\sqrt[4]{10}\\) cannot be compared","hi":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{6}\\) और \\(\\sqrt[4]{10}\\) की तुलना नहीं की जा सकती"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{6} = \\sqrt[4]{10}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"LCM of the orders 3 and 4 is 12<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{6} = 6^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 6^{\\frac{4}{12}} = \\sqrt[12]{1296}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[4]{10} = 10^{\\frac{1}{4}} = 10^{\\frac{3}{12}} = \\sqrt[12]{1000}\\)<br>Since \\(1296 \\gt 1000\\), \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt[3]{6} \\gt \\sqrt[4]{10}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\sqrt[3]{6} \\gt \\sqrt[4]{10}\\).</b>","hi":"कोटियों 3 और 4 का लघुत्तम समापवर्त्य 12 है<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{6} = 6^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 6^{\\frac{4}{12}} = \\sqrt[12]{1296}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[4]{10} = 10^{\\frac{1}{4}} = 10^{\\frac{3}{12}} = \\sqrt[12]{1000}\\)<br>चूँकि \\(1296 \\gt 1000\\), अतः \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt[3]{6} \\gt \\sqrt[4]{10}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\sqrt[3]{6} \\gt \\sqrt[4]{10}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073153","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two intersecting circles have a common tangent line and a common chord. The line segment joining the centers of these two circles is always perpendicular to: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो प्रतिच्छेदी वृत्तों की एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा और एक उभयनिष्ठ जीवा होती है। इन दोनों वृत्तों के केंद्रों को जोड़ने वाला रेखाखंड सदैव किसके लंबवत होता है: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The common tangent line, only if the two circles have equal radii.","hi":"उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा के, केवल तब जब दोनों वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ बराबर हों।"},"2":{"en":"The common chord of the two circles.","hi":"दोनों वृत्तों की उभयनिष्ठ जीवा के।"},"3":{"en":"The tangent drawn from an external point to only one circle.","hi":"केवल एक वृत्त के लिए बाह्य बिंदु से खींची गई स्पर्श रेखा के।"},"4":{"en":"The common tangent line, regardless of the radii of the circles.","hi":"उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा के, वृत्तों की त्रिज्याओं की परवाह किए बिना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"105\" r=\"52\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"105\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M25 105H218\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M125 66.5V143.5\"/><path d=\"M125 97H133V105\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O′</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O′</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">common chord</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">common chord</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">line of centres</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">line of centres</text></g></svg><br>The common chord AB is the perpendicular bisector of the segment joining the centres O and O'<br>So the line of centres is perpendicular to the common chord<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{The common chord of the two circles}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The common chord of the two circles.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"105\" r=\"52\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"105\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M25 105H218\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M125 66.5V143.5\"/><path d=\"M125 97H133V105\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O′</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O′</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">common chord</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">common chord</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">line of centres</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">line of centres</text></g></svg><br>उभयनिष्ठ जीवा AB, केंद्रों O और O' को जोड़ने वाले रेखाखंड का लंब समद्विभाजक है<br>अतः केंद्रों की रेखा उभयनिष्ठ जीवा के लंबवत है<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{दोनों वृत्तों की उभयनिष्ठ जीवा के}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): दोनों वृत्तों की उभयनिष्ठ जीवा के। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073154","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A laptop is available for ₹66, 550 by cash payment or by paying ₹50, 000 as down payment and the balance in three equal annual instalments. If interest is charged at 10% per annum compounded annually, what is the amount of each instalment? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लैपटॉप ₹66, 550 नकद भुगतान पर या ₹50, 000 अग्रिम भुगतान और शेष राशि तीन समान वार्षिक किश्तों में देकर उपलब्ध है। यदि ब्याज 10% वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि दर से लिया जाता है, तो प्रत्येक किश्त की राशि कितनी है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6, 655"},"2":{"en":"₹6, 500"},"3":{"en":"₹6, 750"},"4":{"en":"₹6, 810"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Balance after down payment = \\(66550 - 50000 = 16550\\)<br>Present value of three equal instalments at 10% = 16550<br>\\(x\\left(\\frac{1}{1.1} + \\frac{1}{1.21} + \\frac{1}{1.331}\\right) = 16550\\)<br>\\(x(0.909091 + 0.826446 + 0.751315) = 16550\\)<br>\\(x \\times 2.486852 = 16550 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{6655}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹6, 655.</b>","hi":"अग्रिम भुगतान के बाद शेष = \\(66550 - 50000 = 16550\\)<br>10% पर तीन समान किश्तों का वर्तमान मूल्य = 16550<br>\\(x\\left(\\frac{1}{1.1} + \\frac{1}{1.21} + \\frac{1}{1.331}\\right) = 16550\\)<br>\\(x(0.909091 + 0.826446 + 0.751315) = 16550\\)<br>\\(x \\times 2.486852 = 16550 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{6655}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹6, 655 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073155","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Boxes A, B and C initially contain items in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. A gives one-third of its items to B; B then gives one-fourth of its new total to C. What is the final ratio A : B : C? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बक्से A, B और C में प्रारंभ में वस्तुएँ 3 : 4 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। A अपनी वस्तुओं का एक-तिहाई B को देता है; फिर B अपनी नई कुल संख्या का एक-चौथाई C को देता है। अंतिम अनुपात A : B : C क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 : 20 : 24"},"2":{"en":"6 : 15 : 25"},"3":{"en":"8 : 15 : 25"},"4":{"en":"8 : 15 : 20"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Start with A = 3, B = 4, C = 5<br>A gives 1 to B: A = 2, B = 5, C = 5<br>B gives one-fourth of 5 = 1.25 to C: B = 3.75, C = 6.25<br>Ratio = \\(2 : 3.75 : 6.25 = 8 : 15 : 25\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{8 : 15 : 25}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8 : 15 : 25.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभ में A = 3, B = 4, C = 5<br>A, B को 1 देता है: A = 2, B = 5, C = 5<br>B, 5 का एक-चौथाई = 1.25 C को देता है: B = 3.75, C = 6.25<br>अनुपात = \\(2 : 3.75 : 6.25 = 8 : 15 : 25\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{8 : 15 : 25}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 : 15 : 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, remain one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats. Constructed over 4,500 years ago, these geometric marvels continue to baffle engineers, historians, and archaeologists alike. Despite centuries of scrutiny, the exact methodologies employed in their construction elude definitive explanation.<br><br>The prevailing theories suggest that a combination of ingenuity, rudimentary tools, and sheer human determination enabled the transportation and placement of multi-ton limestone blocks with astonishing precision. However, emerging hypotheses propose that the ancient Egyptians may have leveraged techniques far more sophisticated than previously acknowledged, including the potential use of water to reduce friction on desert sands or the employment of lost materials like early forms of concrete.<br><br>Beyond the mechanics of their assembly, the pyramids encapsulate profound cultural and religious significance. They were not merely tombs, but cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence into the afterlife, aligning meticulously with celestial bodies to reflect a deeper metaphysical order. The internal labyrinths, adorned with cryptic hieroglyphs and symbolic chambers, further attest to a civilization whose understanding of mathematics, astronomy, and theology was remarkably advanced.<br><br>Today, while modern technology such as satellite imaging and muon radiography peels back some layers of mystery, the pyramids still guard many of their secrets. They stand not merely as relics of a bygone era, but as enduring testaments to humanity's timeless pursuit of greatness, ingenuity, and the eternal enigma of existence itself.<br><br><br>Identify the correct form of the verb that should fill the blank:<br>“The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, ___ one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats.” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"is"},"2":{"en":"was"},"3":{"en":"are"},"4":{"en":"were"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The plural subject “the pyramids” takes the plural verb “are.”</b><br>The intervening descriptive phrase does not change subject–verb agreement.<br>The sentence states a present general fact.<br>“Is” and “was” are singular; “were” incorrectly shifts to past.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): are.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, remain one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats. Constructed over 4,500 years ago, these geometric marvels continue to baffle engineers, historians, and archaeologists alike. Despite centuries of scrutiny, the exact methodologies employed in their construction elude definitive explanation.<br><br>The prevailing theories suggest that a combination of ingenuity, rudimentary tools, and sheer human determination enabled the transportation and placement of multi-ton limestone blocks with astonishing precision. However, emerging hypotheses propose that the ancient Egyptians may have leveraged techniques far more sophisticated than previously acknowledged, including the potential use of water to reduce friction on desert sands or the employment of lost materials like early forms of concrete.<br><br>Beyond the mechanics of their assembly, the pyramids encapsulate profound cultural and religious significance. They were not merely tombs, but cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence into the afterlife, aligning meticulously with celestial bodies to reflect a deeper metaphysical order. The internal labyrinths, adorned with cryptic hieroglyphs and symbolic chambers, further attest to a civilization whose understanding of mathematics, astronomy, and theology was remarkably advanced.<br><br>Today, while modern technology such as satellite imaging and muon radiography peels back some layers of mystery, the pyramids still guard many of their secrets. They stand not merely as relics of a bygone era, but as enduring testaments to humanity's timeless pursuit of greatness, ingenuity, and the eternal enigma of existence itself.<br><br><br>Choose the correct conjunction to complete the sentence:<br>“The pyramids were not merely tombs, ___ cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence.” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"but"},"2":{"en":"and"},"3":{"en":"or"},"4":{"en":"for"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The correlative pair is “not merely … but.”</b><br>The pyramids served not only as tombs but also as cosmic monuments.<br>“And” does not complete the contrastive construction.<br>“Or” presents an alternative, and “for” gives a reason.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): but.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, remain one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats. Constructed over 4,500 years ago, these geometric marvels continue to baffle engineers, historians, and archaeologists alike. Despite centuries of scrutiny, the exact methodologies employed in their construction elude definitive explanation.<br><br>The prevailing theories suggest that a combination of ingenuity, rudimentary tools, and sheer human determination enabled the transportation and placement of multi-ton limestone blocks with astonishing precision. However, emerging hypotheses propose that the ancient Egyptians may have leveraged techniques far more sophisticated than previously acknowledged, including the potential use of water to reduce friction on desert sands or the employment of lost materials like early forms of concrete.<br><br>Beyond the mechanics of their assembly, the pyramids encapsulate profound cultural and religious significance. They were not merely tombs, but cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence into the afterlife, aligning meticulously with celestial bodies to reflect a deeper metaphysical order. The internal labyrinths, adorned with cryptic hieroglyphs and symbolic chambers, further attest to a civilization whose understanding of mathematics, astronomy, and theology was remarkably advanced.<br><br>Today, while modern technology such as satellite imaging and muon radiography peels back some layers of mystery, the pyramids still guard many of their secrets. They stand not merely as relics of a bygone era, but as enduring testaments to humanity's timeless pursuit of greatness, ingenuity, and the eternal enigma of existence itself.<br><br><br>What is the meaning of “transcendence” as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fall from power"},"2":{"en":"Rising above normal limits"},"3":{"en":"Physical transformation"},"4":{"en":"Intellectual decline"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Transcendence (पारगमन) = rising beyond ordinary physical or spiritual limits.</b><br>The pyramids were intended to secure the pharaohs’ passage beyond earthly life.<br>Fall from power and intellectual decline are opposite ideas.<br>Physical transformation alone does not capture the spiritual ascent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Rising above normal limits.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, remain one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats. Constructed over 4,500 years ago, these geometric marvels continue to baffle engineers, historians, and archaeologists alike. Despite centuries of scrutiny, the exact methodologies employed in their construction elude definitive explanation.<br><br>The prevailing theories suggest that a combination of ingenuity, rudimentary tools, and sheer human determination enabled the transportation and placement of multi-ton limestone blocks with astonishing precision. However, emerging hypotheses propose that the ancient Egyptians may have leveraged techniques far more sophisticated than previously acknowledged, including the potential use of water to reduce friction on desert sands or the employment of lost materials like early forms of concrete.<br><br>Beyond the mechanics of their assembly, the pyramids encapsulate profound cultural and religious significance. They were not merely tombs, but cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence into the afterlife, aligning meticulously with celestial bodies to reflect a deeper metaphysical order. The internal labyrinths, adorned with cryptic hieroglyphs and symbolic chambers, further attest to a civilization whose understanding of mathematics, astronomy, and theology was remarkably advanced.<br><br>Today, while modern technology such as satellite imaging and muon radiography peels back some layers of mystery, the pyramids still guard many of their secrets. They stand not merely as relics of a bygone era, but as enduring testaments to humanity's timeless pursuit of greatness, ingenuity, and the eternal enigma of existence itself.<br><br><br>Which word in the passage is closest in meaning to “hypotheses”? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Proofs"},"2":{"en":"Theories"},"3":{"en":"Facts"},"4":{"en":"Questions"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Hypotheses (परिकल्पनाएँ) = proposed explanations requiring further evidence.</b><br>The passage itself mentions “prevailing theories” and “emerging hypotheses.”<br>“Theories” is the closest synonym.<br>Proofs and facts imply established truth; questions do not provide explanations.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Theories.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The pyramids, most famously epitomized by the colossal structures at Giza, remain one of humanity's most astonishing architectural feats. Constructed over 4,500 years ago, these geometric marvels continue to baffle engineers, historians, and archaeologists alike. Despite centuries of scrutiny, the exact methodologies employed in their construction elude definitive explanation.<br><br>The prevailing theories suggest that a combination of ingenuity, rudimentary tools, and sheer human determination enabled the transportation and placement of multi-ton limestone blocks with astonishing precision. However, emerging hypotheses propose that the ancient Egyptians may have leveraged techniques far more sophisticated than previously acknowledged, including the potential use of water to reduce friction on desert sands or the employment of lost materials like early forms of concrete.<br><br>Beyond the mechanics of their assembly, the pyramids encapsulate profound cultural and religious significance. They were not merely tombs, but cosmic monuments designed to ensure the pharaohs’ transcendence into the afterlife, aligning meticulously with celestial bodies to reflect a deeper metaphysical order. The internal labyrinths, adorned with cryptic hieroglyphs and symbolic chambers, further attest to a civilization whose understanding of mathematics, astronomy, and theology was remarkably advanced.<br><br>Today, while modern technology such as satellite imaging and muon radiography peels back some layers of mystery, the pyramids still guard many of their secrets. They stand not merely as relics of a bygone era, but as enduring testaments to humanity's timeless pursuit of greatness, ingenuity, and the eternal enigma of existence itself.<br><br><br>According to the passage, which of the following best describes the primary cultural significance of the pyramids? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They symbolized military power."},"2":{"en":"They represent spiritual power."},"3":{"en":"They represented a metaphysical journey linked to celestial alignment."},"4":{"en":"They were primarily built to showcase wealth to rival civilizations."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The pyramids ensured transcendence into the afterlife and aligned with celestial bodies.</b><br>They reflected a metaphysical order rather than merely serving as tombs.<br>Military power, general spiritual power and displays of wealth are not the passage’s primary emphasis.<br>The metaphysical journey and celestial alignment are explicitly linked.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They represented a metaphysical journey linked to celestial alignment.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate tense of the underlined words.<br>While he <b>deliver</b> his speech, the audience <b>listened</b> attentively. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"delivers, listens"},"2":{"en":"delivered, listened"},"3":{"en":"was delivering, was listening"},"4":{"en":"had delivered, had listened"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Two simultaneous past actions can use past continuous in both clauses.</b><br>“While he was delivering …, the audience was listening …” describes concurrent ongoing actions.<br>A shifts to present; B uses simple past rather than the intended continuous background.<br>D uses past perfect, which would place both actions before another past event.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): was delivering, was listening.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. <b>ELOQUENCE</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Halting"},"2":{"en":"Hesitant"},"3":{"en":"Fluency"},"4":{"en":"Stammering"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Eloquence (वाक्पटुता) = fluent, forceful and persuasive expression.</b><br><b>Halting (अटका हुआ)</b> = hesitant in speech<br><b>Hesitant (संकोची)</b> = uncertain<br><b>Fluency (प्रवाहपूर्णता)</b> = smooth expression ✔<br><b>Stammering (हकलाना)</b> = involuntary repetition of sounds; synonyms: articulacy, rhetoric.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Fluency.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. <b>SYCOPHANT</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Advisor"},"2":{"en":"Flatterer"},"3":{"en":"Companion"},"4":{"en":"Advocate"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Sycophant (चापलूस) = a servile flatterer seeking advantage.</b><br><b>Advisor (सलाहकार)</b> = one who gives advice<br><b>Flatterer (खुशामदी)</b> = one who praises insincerely ✔<br><b>Companion (साथी)</b> = associate; <b>advocate (समर्थक)</b> = supporter; synonyms: toady, bootlicker.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Flatterer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Rehabilitation</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Recuperation"},"2":{"en":"Deterioration"},"3":{"en":"Restoration"},"4":{"en":"Adjustment"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rehabilitation (पुनर्वास) = restoration to health or normal functioning.</b><br><b>Recuperation (स्वास्थ्यलाभ)</b> = recovery<br><b>Deterioration (गिरावट)</b> = worsening ✔<br><b>Restoration (पुनर्स्थापना)</b> = repair; <b>adjustment (समायोजन)</b> = adaptation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Deterioration.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the below given passive voice sentence into active voice.<br>“The national award was presented to the artist by the President of India”. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The President of India presents the national award to the artist"},"2":{"en":"The President of India is presenting the national award to the artist"},"3":{"en":"The President of India presented the national award to the artist"},"4":{"en":"The President of India has presented the national award to the artist"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past passive becomes simple past active.</b><br>The agent “the President of India” becomes the subject.<br>“Was presented” becomes “presented,” and the artist remains the recipient.<br>The other options change the tense or aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The President of India presented the national award to the artist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) to ensure faster delivery<br>B) across departments<br>C) services are being digitised<br>D) through the Digital India program [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D-B-C-A"},"2":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"3":{"en":"B-D-A-C"},"4":{"en":"A-C-B-D"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-B-D-A</b><br>C supplies the main clause: services are being digitised.<br>B identifies their distribution across departments, and D names the programme.<br>A concludes with the purpose: ensuring faster delivery.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): C-B-D-A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of the following words is misspelt? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Juxtaposition"},"2":{"en":"Sychophant"},"3":{"en":"Obfuscate"},"4":{"en":"Quandary"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Sycophant (चापलूस) = a servile flatterer.</b><br><b>Sychophant</b> omits “o” after “sych.”<br><b>Juxtaposition</b> = placing close together for contrast.<br><b>Obfuscate</b> = make unclear; <b>quandary</b> = dilemma; both are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Sychophant.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Which term refers to “The portrayal of realistic and detailed scenes of everyday life, often focusing on mundane or trivial subjects”? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Impressionism"},"2":{"en":"Surrealism"},"3":{"en":"Realism"},"4":{"en":"Verism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Realism (यथार्थवाद) = the portrayal of everyday life and ordinary people as they are, including mundane subjects.</b><br>The definition stresses realistic, detailed scenes of everyday life and ordinary subjects, which is the defining feature of realism.<br>Impressionism = capturing fleeting impressions of light and colour<br>Surrealism = dreamlike or irrational imagery<br>Verism = an extreme, often harsh form of realism; it is a narrower term than the general one asked here<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Realism.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“The sword of Damocles” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A lucky opportunity"},"2":{"en":"A constant threat hanging over someone"},"3":{"en":"A weapon of power"},"4":{"en":"A tool for justice"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>The sword of Damocles (सिर पर लटकता खतरा) = an ever-present impending danger.</b><br>Example: “The threat of closure hung like the sword of Damocles over the workers.”<br>It does not denote luck, power or justice.<br>The image is of danger suspended overhead.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A constant threat hanging over someone.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>His recent paper is as ___ as any ever published in the journal's history. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"insightful"},"2":{"en":"more insightful"},"3":{"en":"most insightful"},"4":{"en":"insightfully"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “As + positive adjective + as” expresses equality.</b><br>“As insightful as” compares the paper with any other in the journal’s history.<br>Comparative and superlative forms do not fit this construction.<br>“Insightfully” is an adverb, but an adjective is required.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): insightful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The speaker's tone, marked by sarcastic inflections, stood in stark ___ to the solemnity of the occasion. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"proportion"},"2":{"en":"contrast"},"3":{"en":"parallel"},"4":{"en":"deference"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Stand in stark contrast to” = be strikingly different from.</b><br>Sarcasm contrasted sharply with the solemn occasion.<br>“Proportion” concerns relative size, and “parallel” implies similarity.<br>“Deference” means respectful submission.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): contrast.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To have a chip on one's shoulder” mean? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To be overly cautious"},"2":{"en":"To be very confident in one's abilities"},"3":{"en":"To be unaware of one's surroundings"},"4":{"en":"To hold a grudge or be easily offended"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Have a chip on one’s shoulder (शिकायत का भाव रखना) = remain resentful or easily offended.</b><br>Example: “He has a chip on his shoulder about not being promoted.”<br>Caution, confidence and unawareness are unrelated.<br>The idiom centres on a lingering grievance.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): To hold a grudge or be easily offended.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>The research paper was full of errors because the data <b>is not verified</b> by any expert. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"has not been verified"},"2":{"en":"was not verified"},"3":{"en":"had not been verified"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past passive matches the past-time reporting context.</b><br>Correct wording: “the data <b>was not verified</b> by any expert.”<br>“Is not verified” incorrectly shifts to present.<br>Present perfect and past perfect create unnecessary time relationships.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): was not verified.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Choose the correctly spelt word that best completes the sentence meaningfully.<br>The company's new marketing strategy has received ___ feedback from customers. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"positiv"},"2":{"en":"posotive"},"3":{"en":"positve"},"4":{"en":"positive"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Positive (सकारात्मक) = favourable or approving.</b><br>The correct spelling is “positive.”<br><b>Positiv</b> omits final “e”; <b>posotive</b> misplaces “o.”<br><b>Positve</b> omits “i.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): positive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. The sample is then placed for testing.<br>2. A detailed report is generated after analysis.<br>3. The test begins after the equipment is confirmed ready.<br>4. The technician calibrates the instrument using standard samples. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-4-3-2"},"2":{"en":"4-1-3-2"},"3":{"en":"3-4-2-1"},"4":{"en":"2-1-4-3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-1-3-2</b><br>The technician first calibrates the instrument, then places the sample for testing.<br>The test begins after readiness is confirmed.<br>A detailed report is generated last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4-1-3-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. The Panchayat submits its annual development plan as per the bottom-up planning mandate.<br>2. Delays in fund release from the state treasury lead to stalled work mid-cycle.<br>3. The District Planning Committee forwards the plan to the state department.<br>4. Budget approvals are issued after prolonged scrutiny and conditionalities. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-3-4-2"},"2":{"en":"2-4-3-1"},"3":{"en":"3-1-2-4"},"4":{"en":"4-1-3-2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-4-2</b><br>The Panchayat submits the plan, which the District Planning Committee forwards.<br>Budget approval follows scrutiny and conditions.<br>Treasury delays then stall the work.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1-3-4-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Euphoria</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bliss"},"2":{"en":"Elation"},"3":{"en":"Despair"},"4":{"en":"Joy"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Euphoria (अत्यधिक हर्ष) = intense happiness.</b><br><b>Bliss (परमानंद)</b> = perfect joy<br><b>Elation (हर्षोन्माद)</b> = great happiness<br><b>Despair (निराशा)</b> = complete loss of hope ✔<br><b>Joy (आनंद)</b> = happiness; other antonyms: gloom, misery.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Despair.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a five-year interval term. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Quinquennial"},"2":{"en":"Quinquenniel"},"3":{"en":"Quinquenial"},"4":{"en":"Quinquannial"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Quinquennial (पंचवार्षिक) = occurring every five years or lasting five years.</b><br>The correct spelling is “quinquennial.”<br><b>Quinquenniel</b> reverses the final vowels; <b>quinquenial</b> omits “n.”<br><b>Quinquannial</b> incorrectly uses “a.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Quinquennial.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who is excessively concerned with minor details and rules”. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pedant"},"2":{"en":"Recluse"},"3":{"en":"Egoist"},"4":{"en":"Stoic"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Pedant (पंडिताऊ) = one excessively concerned with formal rules and minor details.</b><br><b>Recluse (एकांतवासी)</b> = a person living in seclusion<br><b>Egoist (अहंवादी)</b> = a self-centred person<br><b>Stoic (स्थिरचित्त)</b> = one who endures hardship without complaint<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Pedant.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The professor gave a long <b>lecture</b> on postmodernism. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The lecture began at 2 PM."},"2":{"en":"The lecture hall was packed."},"3":{"en":"He will lecture the students on discipline."},"4":{"en":"Students attended the lecture daily."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Lecture = an educational talk, or a lengthy reprimand.</b><br>The original uses “lecture” as an academic talk.<br>Option C uses the verbal form meaning to reprimand students about discipline.<br>The other options retain the academic-talk meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He will lecture the students on discipline.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};